# A country's cyber attacks and the learning loop: when effects operations start to pay.
scenario "A country's cyber attacks and the learning loop"
    summary "A country splits its scarce cyber operators between surveillance and attacks, and its researchers
        and analysts serve both. Surveillance pays each day that it runs, but an attack pays only when the
        country uses it, and the use burns its flaws and tools. Attacks teach the country only when it makes
        many of them, and the lessons fade. The model follows the split, the flaws, the lessons and the
        results for 25 years while AI makes attacks cheaper. It shows when military plans start to count on
        cyber attacks."
    horizon 25 years
    timescales leadership.adjust_time, 1 / defenders.calm_rate, 1 / effects_program.forget_rate
    resolution 7 days
    scope "One capable country's cyber force, its surveillance and its attacks, from 2026 for 25 years."
    library "../library"

ai_tools:  @ai_path
    "The AI tools that the country's cyber force can use. They improve over the years that the model follows."
    title "AI tools"
    role environment
    input pace: fraction = 1 in [0, 1]  @ai_pace
        "Share of AI progress that reaches the cyber force"
    input progress_time: years = 5 years in [2 years, 20 years]  @ai_pace
        "Time until AI progress reaches about two thirds of its end"
    input reversal_start: years = 12 years in [1 years, 24 years]  @ai_reversal
        "Time when the costs of attacks start to rise again"
    input reversal_depth: fraction = 0 in [0, 1]  @ai_reversal
        "Share of AI progress that the rise of costs takes back"
    input reversal_time: years = 3 years in [0.5 years, 10 years]  @ai_reversal
        "Time until the rise of costs reaches about two thirds of its end"
    input payload_time: years = 10 years in [2 years, 30 years]  @stage_paths
        "Time until AI progress on payloads reaches about two thirds of its end"
    readonly progress: formula(fraction) = formula(clip(this.pace * (1 - exp(-t / this.progress_time)
        - this.reversal_depth * (1 - exp(-max(t - this.reversal_start, 0 years) / this.reversal_time))), 0,
        1))  @ai_path
        "AI progress that reaches the cyber force's access and the running of its attacks"
    readonly payload_progress: formula(fraction) = formula(clip(this.pace * (1 - exp(-t / this.payload_time)
        - this.reversal_depth * (1 - exp(-max(t - this.reversal_start, 0 years) / this.reversal_time))), 0,
        1))  @stage_paths
        "AI progress that reaches the building of payloads, the review and the approval of an attack and
            damage assessment"

leadership:  @split_basis
    "The country's leaders, who split the country's cyber operators between surveillance and attacks each year
        from the assessed results."
    title "Leaders"
    role operator
    input experts: people = 40535 people in [5000 people, 100000 people]  @experts_pool
        "Cyber experts of the country: researchers, operators and analysts"
    input share_now: fraction = 0.087 in [0.07, 0.16]  @share_today
        "Share of the experts on attacks today"
    input share_floor: fraction = 0.03 in [0.005, 0.06]  @split_limits
        "Smallest share of the operators that the leaders keep on attacks"
    input share_ceiling: fraction = 0.9 in [0.6, 0.95]  @split_limits
        "Largest share of the operators that the leaders put on attacks"
    input adjust_time: years = 3 years in [1 years, 6 years]  @funding_speed
        "Time for the split to move about two thirds of the way to its target"
    input steepness: ratio = 2 in [0.5, 10]  @funding_response
        "Response of the target split to the difference in returns"
    input proportional: bool = false  @funding_forms
        "Funding moves in proportion to the difference in returns"
    input proportional_rate: per_year = 0.5 per_year in [0.1 per_year, 2 per_year]  @funding_forms
        "Rate of a proportional funding response"
    input foresight: fraction = 0 in [0, 1]  @funding_rules
        "Weight that funding gives to the value of the lessons of attacks"
    input discount_rate: per_year = 0.03 per_year in [0.02 per_year, 0.1 per_year]  @discount_rate
        "Discount rate of the future value of lessons"
    input assessment_interval: years = 1 years in [0.5 years, 2 years]  @budget_cycle
        "Time between two assessments of the results"
    input surge_funding: USD2025_bn/yr = 0 USD2025_bn/yr in [0 USD2025_bn/yr, 2 USD2025_bn/yr]  @surge_basis
        "Extra money for attacks in each year of a one-off surge"
    input surge_start: years = 0 years in [0 years, 20 years]  @surge_basis
        "Time when the surge starts"
    input surge_years: years = 4 years in [1 years, 10 years]  @surge_basis
        "Length of the surge"
    input expert_cost: USD2025_m/person/year = 0.42 USD2025_m/person/year in [0.25 USD2025_m/person/year,
        0.6 USD2025_m/person/year]  @expert_cost
        "Cost of one expert for one year"
    attack_share: fraction = operators.share_now in [0.005, 0.95] scale 1  @split_balance
        "Share of the operators on attacks"
    surge: enum[OFF, ON, OVER] = OFF  @surge_basis
        "One-off surge of money for attacks"
    assessment_error: ratio = 0 in [-4, 4] scale 1  @assessment_noise
        "Error of the latest assessment of the value of attacks, in log units"
    next_assessment: years = this.assessment_interval scale 25 years  @budget_cycle
        "Time of the next assessment"
    readonly return_unit: sev/person/year = 1 sev/person/year  @sev_definition
        "Return of one expert on surveillance in 2026"
    readonly surge_experts: formula(people) = formula(this.surge_funding / this.expert_cost if this.surge
        == ON else 0 people)  @surge_basis
        "Experts that the surge pays for"
    readonly attack_experts: formula(people) = formula(this.attack_share * operators.active
        + this.surge_experts)  @split_balance
        "Operators on attacks"
    readonly attack_experts_now: formula(people) = formula(operators.attack_now)  @split_balance
        "Operators on attacks today"
    readonly center: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(max(operators.share_now - this.share_floor,
        0.001) / max(this.share_ceiling - operators.share_now, 0.001)))  @funding_response
        "Log-odds of today's share between the floor and the ceiling"
    readonly assessed_return: formula(sev/person/year) = formula((effects_program.risk_value
        * exp(this.assessment_error + effects_program.assessment_bias) - effects_program.attack_cost)
        / this.attack_experts + this.foresight * effects_program.lesson_value)  @funding_rules
        "Assessed return of one operator on attacks"
    readonly return_gap: formula(ratio) = formula((this.assessed_return - surveillance_program.spying_return)
        / surveillance_program.spying_return)  @funding_rules
        "Difference between the returns of attacks and surveillance, as a share of surveillance's return"
    readonly target_share: formula(fraction) = formula(this.share_floor + (this.share_ceiling
        - this.share_floor) / (1 + exp(-clip(this.steepness * this.return_gap + this.center, -40,
        40))))  @funding_response
        "Share of the experts that the leaders aim to put on attacks"
    readonly room: formula(fraction) = formula(clip(this.attack_share - this.share_floor, 0,
        1) * clip(this.share_ceiling - this.attack_share, 0, 1))  @funding_forms
        "Room of the split between its floor and its ceiling"
    readonly gross_return: formula(ratio) = formula((effects_program.risk_value * exp(this.assessment_error
        + effects_program.assessment_bias) / this.attack_experts + this.foresight
        * effects_program.lesson_value) / surveillance_program.spying_return)  @funding_forms
        "Assessed value of one operator on attacks, before costs, as a share of surveillance's return"
    readonly cost_return: formula(ratio) = formula((effects_program.attack_cost / this.attack_experts
        + surveillance_program.spying_return) / surveillance_program.spying_return)  @funding_forms
        "Costs of one operator on attacks, with the surveillance that the operator does not do, as a share of
            surveillance's return"
    flow rise: SOURCE -> this.attack_share  @funding_response
        "The leaders put more of the experts on attacks."
        request = formula(this.proportional_rate * this.room * this.gross_return if this.proportional
            else this.target_share / this.adjust_time)
        capacity = formula(this.proportional_rate * this.room * this.gross_return if this.proportional
            else this.target_share / this.adjust_time)
    flow fall: this.attack_share -> SINK  @funding_response
        "The leaders put fewer of the experts on attacks."
        request = formula(this.proportional_rate * this.room * this.cost_return if this.proportional
            else this.attack_share / this.adjust_time)
        capacity = formula(this.proportional_rate * this.room * this.cost_return if this.proportional
            else this.attack_share / this.adjust_time)
    surge_begins = event():  @surge_basis
        "A one-off surge of money for attacks starts."
        when t >= this.surge_start and this.surge_funding > 0 USD2025_bn/yr:
            this.surge_begins.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            this.surge = ON
    surge_ends = event():  @surge_basis
        "The surge of money ends."
        when count(this.surge_begins.occurrences) > 0 and since(this.surge_begins) >= this.surge_years:
            this.surge_ends.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            this.surge = OVER
    # The yearly assessment reads the year's results. In the central run its draw is the median, 0.
    assess = event():  @assessment_noise
        "The leaders assess the value of the year's attacks and set the next split."
        when t >= this.next_assessment:
            this.assess.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.assessment_error = clip(effects_program.assessment_spread * normal(0, 1, -4, 4).draw(), -4,
                4)
            this.next_assessment += this.assessment_interval

researchers:  @research_basis
    "The country's experts who find flaws that the defenders do not know and build the tools that use them.
        One group serves both missions, and its work goes to each pool of capabilities as the pool needs it."
    title "Researchers"
    role operator
    input share: fraction = 0.03 in [0.01, 0.1]  @research_share
        "Share of the experts who find flaws and build tools"
    input reserve_time: years = 1 years in [0.1 years, 5 years]  @capability_reserve
        "Years of today's needs that a pool holds unused"
    input supply_time: years = 0.02 years in [0.005 years, 0.25 years]  @capability_reserve
        "Time of asks below which a pool's never-used stock starts to hold back the asks"
    input gain_end: ratio = 10 in [1, 100]  @research_ai
        "Capabilities that a researcher finds in a year at the end of AI progress, as a multiple of today's"
    readonly people: formula(people) = formula(this.share * leadership.experts)  @research_share
        "Researchers"
    readonly need: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(sum(Pool.instances.research_need))  @research_split
        "Capabilities that the pools ask from the researchers in a year"
    readonly need_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(sum(Pool.instances.research_need_now))  @research_split
        "The same need today"
    readonly finds_now: formula(capabilities/person/year) = formula(this.need_now
        / this.people)  @research_yield
        "Capabilities that one researcher finds in a year today"
    readonly finds: formula(capabilities/person/year) = formula(this.finds_now * exp(ai_tools.progress
        * ln(this.gain_end)))  @research_ai
        "Capabilities that one researcher finds in a year"
    readonly output: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(this.people * this.finds)  @research_yield
        "Capabilities that the researchers find in a year"

operators:  @operator_basis
    "The country's operators. On attacks they gain access, move inside the network, prepare the effect and
        execute it. On surveillance they gain access, move inside the network and deploy implants. The leaders
        split them between the two missions, and their hours go first to the operations farthest along."
    title "Operators"
    role operator
    readonly attack_now: formula(people) = formula(effects_program.attacks_now
        * effects_program.operator_cost_now)  @expert_pools
        "Operators on attacks today"
    readonly spy_now: formula(people) = formula(surveillance_program.build_share
        * surveillance_program.experts_now)  @expert_pools
        "Operators on surveillance today: those who gain access and deploy implants"
    readonly people: formula(people) = formula(this.attack_now + this.spy_now)  @expert_pools
        "Operators"
    readonly share_now: formula(fraction) = formula(this.attack_now / this.people)  @expert_pools
        "Share of the operators on attacks today"
    input retrains: bool = false  @workforce
        "The leaders retrain operators who wait for the analysts as analysts"
    input retrain_time: years = 3 years in [0.5 years, 20 years]  @workforce
        "Time for the leaders to move about two thirds of the idle operators into analysis"
    input retrain_efficiency: fraction = 0.5 in [0, 1]  @workforce
        "Analysis work of a retrained operator, as a share of an analyst's"
    retrained_share: fraction = 0 in [0, 0.9] scale 1  @workforce
        "Share of the operators who now do analysis work"
    readonly retrained: formula(people) = formula(this.retrained_share * this.people)  @expert_pools
        "Operators who now do analysis work"
    readonly active: formula(people) = formula((1 - this.retrained_share) * this.people)  @expert_pools
        "Operators who do the work of operations"
    readonly idle: formula(people) = formula(leadership.attack_experts * max(1 - effects_program.starts
        / max(effects_program.wanted_starts, 0.000001 operations/year), 0)
        + surveillance_program.spying_experts * max(1 - surveillance_program.new_accesses
        / max(surveillance_program.builds, 0.000001 accesses/year), 0))  @expert_pools
        "Operators whose hours wait for the analysts to plan their operations"
    flow retrain: SOURCE -> this.retrained_share  @workforce
        "The leaders move idle operators into analysis."
        request = formula(this.idle / this.people / this.retrain_time if this.retrains else 0 per_year)
        capacity = formula(this.idle / this.people / this.retrain_time if this.retrains else 0 per_year)

collection_specialists:  @collection_basis
    "Surveillance's collection specialists. They run collection on the deployed implants, translate, and turn
        the raw take into intelligence."
    title "Collection specialists"
    role operator
    readonly runners_now: formula(people) = formula((1 - surveillance_program.analysis_share)
        * surveillance_program.experts_now - operators.spy_now)  @expert_pools
        "Collection specialists who run collection today"
    readonly processors_now: formula(people) = formula((1 - surveillance_program.plan_share)
        * surveillance_program.analysis_share * surveillance_program.experts_now)  @expert_pools
        "Collection specialists who process the take today"
    readonly people: formula(people) = formula(this.runners_now + this.processors_now)  @expert_pools
        "Collection specialists"

analysts:  @analyst_basis
    "The country's analysts, who plan operations for both missions, assess the damage of attacks and use the
        intelligence. By default they go first to the mission where one more analyst-year is worth more. On
        attacks, damage assessment takes at most its share of the work waiting, and planning the rest."
    title "Analysts"
    role operator
    input load_now: fraction = 0.9 in [0.5, 1]  @analyst_load
        "Share of the analysts' capacity that today's work fills"
    input adjust_time: years = 1 years in [0.25 years, 5 years]  @analyst_split
        "Time for the analysts' split to move about two thirds of the way to the missions' shares of the work"
    readonly people: formula(people) = formula(effects_program.analyst_work_now
        + surveillance_program.planners_now)  @expert_pools
        "Analysts"
    readonly capacity: formula(people) = formula((this.people + operators.retrain_efficiency
        * operators.retrained) / this.load_now)  @analyst_load
        "Analysis work that the analysts can do in a year, in analyst-years at today's pace"
    readonly share_now: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.analyst_work_now
        / this.people)  @analyst_split
        "Share of the analysts on attacks today"
    attack_share: fraction = this.share_now in [0, 1] scale 1  @analyst_split
        "Share of the analysts on attacks"
    readonly asked: formula(people) = formula(effects_program.analysis_asked
        + surveillance_program.analysis_asked)  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work that the two missions have waiting in a year"
    input priority_steepness: ratio = 2 in [0, 10]  @analyst_split
        "Response of the analysts' priority to the ratio of the marginal values of their work"
    readonly attack_margin: formula(sev/operation) = formula(effects_program.risk_value
        / max(effects_program.attacks, 0.001 operations/year) / (1 + effects_program.hits
        / effects_program.saturation) - effects_program.sanctions - effects_program.burned)  @analyst_split
        "Value of one more attack at rest, less its costs"
    readonly attack_margin_value: formula(sev/person/year) = formula(max(this.attack_margin,
        0 sev/operation) / effects_program.analysis_work)  @analyst_split
        "Value of one more analyst-year on attacks, where the analysts limit the attacks"
    readonly spy_margin_value: formula(sev/person/year) = formula(surveillance_program.spying_value
        * surveillance_program.returns_scale * surveillance_program.reach / max(surveillance_program.implants
        + surveillance_program.reach, 1 accesses) / max(surveillance_program.new_accesses
        * surveillance_program.plan_work, 0.001 people))  @analyst_split
        "Value of one more analyst-year on surveillance's planning, where the analysts limit its new accesses"
    readonly priority: formula(fraction) = formula(1 / (1 + exp(-clip(this.priority_steepness
        * ln(max(this.attack_margin_value, 0.000000001 sev/person/year) / max(this.spy_margin_value,
        0.000000001 sev/person/year)), -40, 40))))  @analyst_split
        "Priority of attacks in the analysts' staffing"
    readonly first_attacks: formula(fraction) = formula(min(effects_program.analysis_need / this.people,
        1))  @analyst_split
        "Share of the analysts on attacks when attacks get their work first, with today's slack"
    readonly first_spying: formula(fraction) = formula(max(1 - surveillance_program.analysis_asked
        / this.people, 0))  @analyst_split
        "Share of the analysts on attacks when surveillance gets its work first, with today's slack"
    input by_value: bool = true  @analyst_staffing
        "The analysts go first to the mission where one more analyst-year is worth more"
    input fixed_split: bool = false  @analyst_staffing
        "The analysts' split stays at today's"
    readonly waiting_share: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.analysis_need
        / max(effects_program.analysis_need + surveillance_program.analysis_asked,
        0.001 people))  @analyst_staffing
        "Attacks' share of the analysis work that the two missions need"
    readonly target_share: formula(fraction) = formula(this.share_now if this.fixed_split else this.priority
        * this.first_attacks + (1 - this.priority) * this.first_spying if this.by_value
        else this.waiting_share)  @analyst_staffing
        "Share of the analysts that the staffing rule aims to put on attacks"
    readonly attack_capacity: formula(people) = formula(this.attack_share * this.capacity)  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work that the analysts on attacks can do in a year"
    readonly spy_capacity: formula(people) = formula((1 - this.attack_share) * this.capacity)  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work that the analysts on surveillance can do in a year"
    flow rise: SOURCE -> this.attack_share  @analyst_split
        "Analysts move to attacks where attacks' share of the work waiting is larger than their share."
        request = formula(this.target_share / this.adjust_time)
        capacity = formula(this.target_share / this.adjust_time)
    flow fall: this.attack_share -> SINK  @analyst_split
        "Analysts move to surveillance where it is smaller."
        request = formula(this.attack_share / this.adjust_time)
        capacity = formula(this.attack_share / this.adjust_time)

surveillance_program:  @surveillance_basis
    "The country's surveillance in other countries' networks. Its operators gain access with capabilities from
        the pools, move inside the networks and deploy implants. Its collection specialists run collection on
        the implants and process the take, and its analysts plan new accesses. It loses accesses to the
        defenders and to attacks."
    title "Surveillance"
    role operator
    input returns_scale: fraction = 0.8 in [0.5, 1]  @surveillance_returns
        "Exponent of the value of surveillance in the collection that its analysts process"
    input alert_sensitivity: fraction = 0.3 in [0, 1]  @surveillance_alert
        "Loss of surveillance value for each unit of defender attention or lasting capability"
    input accesses_now: accesses = 85000 accesses in [20000 accesses, 300000 accesses]  @surveillance_accesses
        "Accesses that surveillance holds today"
    input used_now: fraction = 0.12 in [0.05, 0.5]  @surveillance_use
        "Share of its implants that the collection specialists run today"
    input build_share: fraction = 0.05 in [0.02, 0.15]  @surveillance_builders
        "Share of the surveillance experts who gain access and deploy implants"
    input process_time: years = 0.1 years in [0.02 years, 1 years]  @collection_queue
        "Time that the take waits before the collection specialists process it"
    input analysis_share: fraction = 0.5 in [0.2, 0.8]  @surveillance_analysts
        "Share of the surveillance experts who are analysts"
    input plan_share: fraction = 0.1 in [0.02, 0.3]  @surveillance_analysts
        "Share of the analysts' work for surveillance that plans new accesses"
    input plan_target_weight: fraction = 1 in [0, 1]  @surveillance_planning_ai
        "Share of AI's help with each target of an attack that reaches the planning of a new access"
    input analysis_ai_now: fraction = 0.1 in [0, 0.5]  @analysis_ai
        "Share of surveillance's analysis work that AI does today"
    input analysis_ai_end: fraction = 0.6 in [0, 0.9]  @analysis_ai
        "Share of surveillance's analysis work that AI does at the end of AI progress"
    input own_source: fraction = 0.95 in [0.5, 0.995]  @capability_sources
        "Share of surveillance's zero-day needs today that a zero-day it already uses serves"
    input attack_source: fraction = 0.0001 in [0, 0.0005]  @capability_sources
        "Share of surveillance's zero-day needs today that a zero-day an earlier attack used serves"
    input find_share: fraction = 0.02 in [0, 0.3]  @capability_burn
        "Share of the accesses that run on a burned capability that the defenders find"
    input loss_rate: per_year = 0.5 per_year in [0.1 per_year, 2 per_year]  @surveillance_loss
        "Rate at which surveillance loses accesses to the defenders, to patches and to changes"
    input run_ai_now: fraction = 0.3 in [0, 0.9]  @surveillance_ai
        "Share of the work of running accesses that automation does today"
    input run_ai_end: fraction = 0.9 in [0, 0.95]  @surveillance_ai
        "Share of the work of running accesses that AI does at the end of AI progress"
    readonly spying_experts: formula(people) = formula((1 - leadership.attack_share)
        * operators.active)  @split_balance
        "Operators on surveillance"
    readonly spying_experts_now: formula(people) = formula(operators.spy_now)  @split_balance
        "Operators on surveillance today"
    readonly experts_now: formula(people) = formula((1 - leadership.share_now) * leadership.experts
        - researchers.people)  @expert_pools
        "Operators and analysts on surveillance today: the agency's experts who are not researchers"
    readonly planners_now: formula(people) = formula(this.plan_share * this.analysis_share
        * this.experts_now)  @surveillance_analysts
        "Analysts who plan surveillance's new accesses today"
    readonly builds_now: formula(accesses/year) = formula(this.accesses_now
        * this.loss_rate)  @surveillance_builds
        "Accesses that surveillance starts in a year today: those that replace its losses"
    # Today's rest point, step by step along the chain. The defenders also find some accesses through the
    # capabilities that exposed attacks burn, so surveillance holds a little fewer than its builds alone keep.
    readonly held_now: formula(accesses) = formula(this.builds_now / (1 / effects_program.movement_time_now
        + this.loss_rate + access_pool.burn_loss_now))  @surveillance_builds @capability_burn
        "Accesses that surveillance has gained today and that wait for their implant"
    readonly deployed_now: formula(accesses/year) = formula(this.held_now
        / effects_program.movement_time_now)  @surveillance_builds
        "Implants that surveillance deploys in a year today"
    readonly implants_now: formula(accesses) = formula(this.deployed_now / (this.loss_rate
        + access_pool.burn_loss_now + movement_pool.burn_loss_now))  @surveillance_builds @capability_burn
        "Implants that surveillance has deployed today"
    readonly build_work_now: formula(person * years/access) = formula(this.spying_experts_now
        / (effects_program.initial_share * this.builds_now + (1 - effects_program.initial_share)
        * this.deployed_now))  @surveillance_builds
        "Operators' work to gain one access and deploy its implant today: the work that keeps today's
            accesses"
    readonly build_work: formula(person * years/access) = formula(this.build_work_now * access_stage.unit_cost
        / access_stage.unit_cost_now)  @surveillance_builds
        "Operators' work to gain one access and deploy its implant"
    readonly deploy_survival: formula(fraction) = formula(1 / (1 + (this.loss_rate + access_pool.burn_loss)
        * effects_program.movement_time))  @surveillance_builds
        "Share of the accesses gained that live until their implant is deployed"
    readonly builds: formula(accesses/year) = formula(this.spying_experts / (this.initial_work
        + this.deploy_work * this.deploy_survival))  @surveillance_builds
        "Accesses that surveillance's operators can start in a year"
    readonly initial_work: formula(person * years/access) = formula(effects_program.initial_share
        * this.build_work)  @surveillance_priority
        "Operators' work to gain initial access for one access"
    readonly deploy_work: formula(person * years/access) = formula((1 - effects_program.initial_share)
        * this.build_work)  @surveillance_priority
        "Operators' work to move inside one network and deploy one implant"
    # The operators on surveillance deploy implants first, then gain new initial access with the hours left.
    readonly deploy_rate: formula(accesses/year) = formula(min(this.accesses_held
        / effects_program.movement_time, this.spying_experts / this.deploy_work))  @surveillance_priority
        "Implants that surveillance deploys in a year"
    readonly access_hours: formula(people) = formula(max(this.spying_experts - this.deploy_rate
        * this.deploy_work, 0 people))  @surveillance_priority
        "Operators' hours on surveillance left for initial access after deployment"
    readonly access_rate: formula(accesses/year) = formula(min(this.accesses_underway
        / effects_program.initial_time, this.access_hours / this.initial_work))  @surveillance_priority
        "Accesses where surveillance gains initial access in a year"
    readonly run_ai: formula(fraction) = formula(this.run_ai_now + (this.run_ai_end - this.run_ai_now)
        * ai_tools.progress)  @surveillance_ai
        "Share of the work of running accesses that AI does"
    readonly run_cost: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.run_ai + this.run_ai * (effects_program.supervision
        / effects_program.parallel + effects_program.compute / leadership.expert_cost))  @surveillance_ai
        "Work to run one access, as a share of the work by hand"
    readonly run_cost_now: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.run_ai_now + this.run_ai_now
        * (effects_program.supervision / effects_program.parallel_now + effects_program.compute_now
        / leadership.expert_cost))  @surveillance_ai
        "The same share today"
    # The collection specialists process the take first, then run collection on the implants with the hours
    # left. Today they process the take of the implants in use as it comes.
    readonly processed_now: formula(accesses) = formula(this.used_now * this.implants_now)  @surveillance_use
        "Take that the collection specialists process in a year today, in access-years: the implants in use"
    readonly reach_now: formula(accesses) = formula(this.implants_now * this.used_now / (1
        - this.used_now))  @surveillance_use
        "Implants that the collection specialists can run today"
    readonly run_work_now: formula(people/access) = formula(collection_specialists.runners_now
        / this.reach_now)  @surveillance_use
        "Collection specialists for each implant that they can run today"
    readonly run_work: formula(people/access) = formula(this.run_work_now * this.run_cost
        / this.run_cost_now)  @surveillance_ai
        "Collection specialists for each implant that they can run"
    readonly analysis_ai: formula(fraction) = formula(this.analysis_ai_now + (this.analysis_ai_end
        - this.analysis_ai_now) * ai_tools.payload_progress)  @analysis_ai
        "Share of surveillance's analysis work that AI does"
    readonly analysis_cost: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.analysis_ai + this.analysis_ai
        * (effects_program.supervision / effects_program.parallel + effects_program.compute
        / leadership.expert_cost))  @analysis_ai
        "Analysis work of surveillance, as a share of the work by hand"
    readonly analysis_cost_now: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.analysis_ai_now + this.analysis_ai_now
        * (effects_program.supervision / effects_program.parallel_now + effects_program.compute_now
        / leadership.expert_cost))  @analysis_ai
        "The same share today"
    readonly plan_work_now: formula(person * years/access) = formula(this.planners_now
        / this.builds_now)  @surveillance_analysts
        "Analysis work to plan one new access today"
    readonly plan_work: formula(person * years/access) = formula(this.plan_work_now
        * exp(this.plan_target_weight * ln(planning_stage.target_cost / planning_stage.target_cost_now) + (1
        - this.plan_target_weight) * ln(planning_stage.unit_cost
        / planning_stage.unit_cost_now)))  @surveillance_planning_ai
        "Analysis work to plan one new access"
    readonly process_work_now: formula(people/access) = formula(collection_specialists.processors_now
        / this.processed_now)  @surveillance_analysts
        "Collection specialists who process one access-year of take in a year today"
    readonly process_work: formula(people/access) = formula(this.process_work_now * this.analysis_cost
        / this.analysis_cost_now)  @analysis_ai
        "Collection specialists who process one access-year of take in a year"
    readonly processed: formula(accesses) = formula(min(this.collected / this.process_time,
        collection_specialists.people / this.process_work))  @collection_queue
        "Take that the collection specialists process in a year, in access-years"
    readonly run_hours: formula(people) = formula(max(collection_specialists.people - this.processed
        * this.process_work, 0 people))  @collection_queue
        "Collection specialists' hours left to run collection after processing"
    readonly reach: formula(accesses) = formula(this.run_hours / this.run_work)  @surveillance_use
        "Implants that the collection specialists can run"
    readonly used: formula(accesses) = formula(this.implants * this.reach / max(this.implants + this.reach,
        1 accesses))  @surveillance_use
        "Implants that the collection specialists run"
    readonly analysis_asked: formula(people) = formula(this.builds * this.plan_work)  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work that surveillance has waiting in a year: the planning of new accesses"
    readonly new_accesses: formula(accesses/year) = formula(min(this.builds,
        analysts.spy_capacity / this.plan_work) * access_pool.spy_served * movement_pool.spy_served
        * collection_pool.spy_served)  @analyst_split
        "Accesses that surveillance starts in a year: those that its operators can start and its analysts
            plan"
    readonly burned_accesses: formula(accesses/year) = formula(access_pool.burn_loss * (this.accesses_held
        + this.implants) + movement_pool.burn_loss * this.implants)  @capability_burn
        "Accesses that the defenders find in a year through the capabilities that exposed attacks burn"
    readonly burned_accesses_now: formula(accesses/year) = formula(access_pool.burn_loss_now * (this.held_now
        + this.implants_now) + movement_pool.burn_loss_now * this.implants_now)  @capability_burn
        "The same accesses today"
    readonly value_now: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.experts_now
        * leadership.return_unit)  @surveillance_returns
        "Value of surveillance in a year today"
    readonly life_value: formula(sev/access) = formula(this.value_now / (this.accesses_now
        * this.loss_rate))  @capability_burn
        "Value of surveillance that one access gives in its life today"
    readonly spying_value: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.value_now * exp(this.returns_scale
        * ln(max(this.processed, 1e-6 accesses) / this.processed_now)) * exp(-this.alert_sensitivity
        * (defenders.alertness - defenders.alert_now + defenders.hardening)))  @surveillance_returns
        "Value of surveillance in a year"
    readonly spying_return: formula(sev/person/year) = formula(this.spying_value
        / this.spying_experts)  @surveillance_returns
        "Return of one operator on surveillance"
    readonly spying_return_now: formula(sev/person/year) = formula(this.value_now
        / this.spying_experts_now)  @surveillance_returns
        "The same return today"
    # The accesses of surveillance along its chain, and the take that waits. Each starts at today's rest value.
    accesses_underway: accesses = this.builds_now * effects_program.initial_time_now in [0 accesses,
        1000000000 accesses] scale 10000 accesses  @surveillance_loop
        "Accesses where surveillance is gaining initial access"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.access_rate)  @surveillance_loop
    accesses_held: accesses = this.held_now in [0 accesses,
        1000000000 accesses] scale 10000 accesses  @surveillance_loop
        "Accesses that surveillance has gained, while it moves inside the network to deploy their implants"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.deploy_rate + (this.loss_rate + access_pool.burn_loss)
            * this.accesses_held)  @surveillance_loop
    implants: accesses = this.implants_now in [0 accesses,
        1000000000 accesses] scale 10000 accesses  @surveillance_loop
        "Implants that surveillance has deployed and collects from"
        outflow.capacity = formula((this.loss_rate + access_pool.burn_loss + movement_pool.burn_loss)
            * this.implants)  @surveillance_loop
    collected: access * years = this.processed_now * this.process_time in [0 access * years,
        1000000000 access * years] scale 10000 access * years  @collection_queue
        "Take that waits for the collection specialists, in access-years"
    flow start_access: SOURCE -> this.accesses_underway  @surveillance_builds
        "Surveillance starts the accesses that its analysts plan."
        request = formula(this.new_accesses)
        capacity = formula(this.new_accesses)
    # Each step moves in parts, one for each source of the capabilities that it needs, as the steps of attacks
    # do. Initial access needs one capability of access.
    flow access_free: this.accesses_underway -> this.accesses_held  @surveillance_loop @one_day_chance
        "Surveillance gains initial access through known flaws or capabilities that it already uses."
        request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.spy_part_free)
        capacity = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.spy_part_free)
    flow access_kept:  @surveillance_loop @capability_use
        "Surveillance gains initial access with kept capabilities of earlier attacks."
        flow accesses_held: this.accesses_underway -> this.accesses_held
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.spy_part_kept)
        flow access_pool_kept_shared: access_pool.kept_attack -> access_pool.kept_shared
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.spy_part_kept * (1 capabilities/access))
    flow access_new:  @surveillance_loop @capability_use
        "Surveillance gains initial access with capabilities that no one has used."
        flow accesses_held: this.accesses_underway -> this.accesses_held
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.spy_part_new)
        flow access_pool_spy_used: access_pool.fresh -> access_pool.spy_used
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.spy_part_new * (1 capabilities/access))
    # Deployment needs one capability to move inside the network and one to collect, each from its own source.
    flow deploy_free_free: this.accesses_held -> this.implants  @surveillance_loop @one_day_chance
        "Surveillance deploys implants through known flaws or capabilities that it already uses."
        request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_free * collection_pool.spy_part_free)
        capacity = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_free * collection_pool.spy_part_free)
    flow deploy_free_new:  @surveillance_loop @capability_use
        "Surveillance deploys implants with a collection capability that no one has used."
        flow implants: this.accesses_held -> this.implants
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_free * collection_pool.spy_part_new)
        flow collection_pool_spy_used: collection_pool.fresh -> collection_pool.spy_used
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_free * collection_pool.spy_part_new
                * (1 capabilities/access))
    flow deploy_kept_free:  @surveillance_loop @capability_use
        "Surveillance deploys implants with kept capabilities of earlier attacks to move inside the network."
        flow implants: this.accesses_held -> this.implants
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_kept * collection_pool.spy_part_free)
        flow movement_pool_kept_shared: movement_pool.kept_attack -> movement_pool.kept_shared
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_kept * collection_pool.spy_part_free
                * (1 capabilities/access))
    flow deploy_kept_new:  @surveillance_loop @capability_use
        "Surveillance deploys implants with kept capabilities of earlier attacks to move, and a new collection
            capability."
        flow implants: this.accesses_held -> this.implants
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_kept * collection_pool.spy_part_new)
        flow movement_pool_kept_shared: movement_pool.kept_attack -> movement_pool.kept_shared
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_kept * collection_pool.spy_part_new
                * (1 capabilities/access))
        flow collection_pool_spy_used: collection_pool.fresh -> collection_pool.spy_used
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_kept * collection_pool.spy_part_new
                * (1 capabilities/access))
    flow deploy_new_free:  @surveillance_loop @capability_use
        "Surveillance deploys implants with a capability to move inside the network that no one has used."
        flow implants: this.accesses_held -> this.implants
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_new * collection_pool.spy_part_free)
        flow movement_pool_spy_used: movement_pool.fresh -> movement_pool.spy_used
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_new * collection_pool.spy_part_free
                * (1 capabilities/access))
    flow deploy_new_new:  @surveillance_loop @capability_use
        "Surveillance deploys implants with new capabilities to move and to collect."
        flow implants: this.accesses_held -> this.implants
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_new * collection_pool.spy_part_new)
        flow movement_pool_spy_used: movement_pool.fresh -> movement_pool.spy_used
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_new * collection_pool.spy_part_new
                * (1 capabilities/access))
        flow collection_pool_spy_used: collection_pool.fresh -> collection_pool.spy_used
            request = formula(this.deploy_rate * movement_pool.spy_part_new * collection_pool.spy_part_new
                * (1 capabilities/access))
    flow access_lost: this.accesses_held -> SINK  @surveillance_loss
        "Surveillance loses accesses to the defenders, to patches and to changes."
        request = formula(this.loss_rate * this.accesses_held)
        capacity = formula(this.loss_rate * this.accesses_held)
    flow access_burned: this.accesses_held -> SINK  @capability_burn
        "The defenders find accesses through the capabilities that exposed attacks burn."
        request = formula(access_pool.burn_loss * this.accesses_held)
        capacity = formula(access_pool.burn_loss * this.accesses_held)
    flow implant_lost: this.implants -> SINK  @surveillance_loss
        "Surveillance loses implants to the defenders, to patches and to changes."
        request = formula(this.loss_rate * this.implants)
        capacity = formula(this.loss_rate * this.implants)
    flow implant_burned: this.implants -> SINK  @capability_burn
        "The defenders find implants through the capabilities that exposed attacks burn."
        request = formula((access_pool.burn_loss + movement_pool.burn_loss) * this.implants)
        capacity = formula((access_pool.burn_loss + movement_pool.burn_loss) * this.implants)
    flow collect: SOURCE -> this.collected  @collection_queue
        "The collection specialists collect the take of the implants that they run: one access-year of take
            for each implant-year."
        request = formula(this.used)
        capacity = formula(this.used)
    flow process: this.collected -> SINK  @collection_queue
        "The collection specialists process the take into intelligence."
        request = formula(this.processed)
        capacity = formula(this.processed)

defenders:  @defender_basis
    "The defenders of the target networks in other countries. Their attention follows the threat flow that
        they answer and fades within months, they fix what attacks expose, and their lasting capability can
        grow."
    title "Defenders"
    role responder
    input alert_now: ratio = 0.05 in [0, 0.2]  @alertness_today
        "Attention of the defenders today, as a loss of log-odds of an attack's success"
    input calm_rate: per_year = 2 per_year in [1 per_year, 3 per_year]  @alertness_fades
        "Rate at which the attention of the defenders fades"
    input force_share: fraction = 0.05 in [0.01, 0.3]  @threat_flow
        "Share of the threat flow that the defenders answer that comes from the force's attacks today"
    input attention_cap: ratio = 6 in [2, 20]  @attention_cap
        "Most attention that the threat flow can draw, as a multiple of today's"
    input hardening_rate: per_year = 0 per_year in [0 per_year, 0.15 per_year]  @hardening
        "Yearly gain of the defenders' lasting capability, as a loss of log-odds of an attack's success"
    input ai_hardening: ratio = 0 in [0, 1.5]  @defender_ai
        "Loss of log-odds of an attack's success that the defenders' AI gives at the end of AI progress"
    input discovery_now: per_year = 0.057 per_year in [0 per_year, 0.145 per_year]  @loss_routes
        "Share of the force's stockpiled flaws that others find on their own and disclose in a year, today"
    input use_discovery_now: per_year = 1.08 per_year in [0.057 per_year, 2 per_year]  @loss_routes
        "The same share of the flaws that the force has in use on targets, where defenders can see them at
            work"
    input patch_now: per_year = 0.044 per_year in [0 per_year, 0.1 per_year]  @loss_routes
        "Share of the flaws that patches and code changes made for other reasons close in a year, today"
    input irrelevance_now: per_year = 0.044 per_year in [0 per_year, 0.1 per_year]  @loss_routes
        "Share of the flaws whose systems leave service or stop mattering in a year"
    input close_gain: ratio = 2 in [0, 5]  @rediscovery
        "Growth of discovery and patching at the end of AI progress, as a multiple of today's rates"
    input within_now: fraction = 0.85 in [0.5, 1]  @outcome_correlation
        "Correlation of the outcomes on the targets of one attack today"
    input fix_rate: per_year = 1.5 per_year in [0.2 per_year, 30 per_year]  @known_flaws
        "Rate at which the defenders fix a known flaw on a target"
    input residual: fraction = 0.25 in [0.05, 0.5]  @known_flaws
        "Share of targets on which a known flaw stays open"
    input common_spread: ratio = 0.3 in [0.1, 0.46]  @common_factor
        "Spread of the log-odds of a plan's success from the defenders that all of its attacks face"
    input shared_failure: fraction = 0.05 in [0, 0.3]  @shared_failure
        "Chance that a step that the attacks of a plan share fails at its start"
    input failure_rate: per_year = 0.6 per_year in [0 per_year, 3 per_year]  @shared_failure
        "Rate at which the defenders find and stop a step that the attacks of a plan share"
    readonly threat: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.force_share + this.force_share
        * effects_program.made_targets / (effects_program.attacks_now
        * effects_program.targets_now))  @threat_flow
        "Threat flow that the defenders answer, as a multiple of today's"
    # Attention saturates: it rises with the threat flow towards its cap, and today's threat draws today's.
    readonly attention_target: formula(ratio) = formula(this.alert_now * this.attention_cap * this.threat
        / (this.threat + this.attention_cap - 1))  @attention_cap
        "Attention that the threat flow draws"
    readonly hardening: formula(ratio) = formula(this.hardening_rate * t + this.ai_hardening
        * ai_tools.progress)  @hardening
        "Loss of log-odds of an attack's success from the defenders' lasting gains"
    readonly closing: formula(ratio) = formula(1 + this.close_gain * ai_tools.progress)  @rediscovery
        "Discovery and patching as a multiple of today's: AI helps the defenders find and close flaws"
    readonly rediscovery_now: formula(per_year) = formula(this.discovery_now + this.patch_now
        + this.irrelevance_now)  @loss_routes
        "Rate at which a stockpiled flaw is lost today, by every route"
    readonly rediscovery: formula(per_year) = formula((this.discovery_now + this.patch_now) * this.closing
        + this.irrelevance_now)  @loss_routes @rediscovery
        "Rate at which a flaw that the force holds unused is lost: found, patched or no longer relevant"
    readonly use_rediscovery_now: formula(per_year) = formula(this.use_discovery_now + this.patch_now
        + this.irrelevance_now)  @loss_routes
        "The same rate of a flaw in use today"
    readonly use_rediscovery: formula(per_year) = formula((this.use_discovery_now + this.patch_now)
        * this.closing + this.irrelevance_now)  @loss_routes @rediscovery
        "Rate at which a flaw that the force uses on targets is lost"
    # Attention is a loss of log-odds; the odds of success are clipped at 40, so it needs no higher value.
    alertness: ratio = this.alert_now in [0, 40] scale 1  @alertness_balance
        "Attention of the defenders, as a loss of log-odds of an attack's success"
    flow alert: SOURCE -> this.alertness  @attention_cap
        "The threat flow draws the defenders' attention."
        request = formula(this.calm_rate * this.attention_target)
        capacity = formula(this.calm_rate * this.attention_target)
    flow calm: this.alertness -> SINK  @alertness_fades
        "The attention of the defenders fades."
        request = formula(this.alertness * this.calm_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.alertness * this.calm_rate)

other_states:  @politics_basis
    "The other countries that attribute attacks and answer them with sanctions or replies."
    title "Other countries"
    role environment
    input sanction_cost: sev/operation = 10 sev/operation in [1 sev/operation,
        100 sev/operation]  @sanction_cost
        "Cost of the sanctions and replies that one attributed attack draws"
    input escalation: years/operation = 0 years/operation in [0 years/operation,
        0.01 years/operation]  @escalation
        "Growth of the cost of sanctions with the attributed attacks in a year"
    readonly attribution: formula(fraction) = formula(1
        - exp(sum(Channel.instances.miss)))  @attribution_channels
        "Chance that other countries attribute an attack to the country"
    readonly attribution_now: formula(fraction) = formula(1
        - exp(sum(Channel.instances.miss_now)))  @attribution_channels
        "Chance today that other countries attribute an attack to the country"

military_planners:  @planning_basis
    "The country's military planners, who build plans around cyber attacks only when a plan of attacks gives
        its intended effect reliably."
    title "Military planners"
    role operator
    input tolerance: fraction = 0.25 in [0.2, 0.5]  @plan_tolerance
        "Shortfall from the planned share of targets hit that the planners accept"
    input acceptance: fraction = 0.8 in [0.75, 0.95]  @plan_tolerance
        "Chance of meeting the plan that the planners need"
    input two_sided: bool = false  @plan_tolerance
        "A plan also fails when its attacks hit more than the tolerance above the planned share"
    input objective_share: fraction = 0.2 in [0.05, 1]  @objective_share
        "Share of the force's attacks that can serve one objective"
    input forecast_floor: ratio = 0.1 in [0.1, 0.3]  @forecast_error
        "Error of the planners' forecast of the share of targets hit that lessons do not remove"
    input passes_needed: ratio = 3 in [1, 10]  @doctrine_time
        "Planning reviews in a row that a plan must pass before plans count on cyber attacks"
    input misses_needed: ratio = 2 in [1, 6]  @doctrine_lapse
        "Planning reviews in a row that every plan must miss before plans stop counting on cyber attacks"
    input review_interval: years = 1 years in [0.5 years, 2 years]  @doctrine_time
        "Time between two planning reviews"
    input doctrine_value: fraction = 0 in [0, 1]  @doctrine_feedback
        "Extra value of each effect once plans count on cyber attacks"
    input war: bool = false  @wartime
        "The country goes to war"
    input war_start: years = 0 years in [0 years, 24 years]  @wartime
        "Time when the war starts"
    input war_review_interval: years = 0.25 years in [0.1 years, 1 years]  @wartime
        "Time between two planning reviews in war"
    tempo: enum[PEACE, WAR] = PEACE  @wartime
        "Tempo of the country's operations"
    next_review: years = this.review_interval scale 25 years  @doctrine_time
        "Time of the next planning review"
    passes_in_a_row: ratio = 0 in [0, 1000] scale 10  @doctrine_time
        "Planning reviews in a row that a plan passes"
    misses_in_a_row: ratio = 0 in [0, 1000] scale 10  @doctrine_lapse
        "Planning reviews in a row that every plan misses"
    doctrine: enum[NONE, FORMED, LAPSED] = NONE  @doctrine_time
        "Plans that count on cyber attacks"
    formed_length: days = 0 days in [0 days, 100 days] scale 30 days  @plan_test
        "Length of the plan that doctrine last formed around"
    readonly forecast_spread: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt(this.forecast_floor ** 2 + (1
        - effects_program.success) / effects_program.success / (effects_program.know_how / (1 targets)
        + 1)))  @forecast_error
        "Error of the planners' forecast of the share of targets hit, as a share of it"
    readonly plan_error: formula(ratio) = formula((1 - this.tolerance)
        * this.forecast_spread)  @forecast_error
        "Spread of the threshold that the forecast error gives a plan, as a share of the planned share"
    readonly best_chance: formula(fraction) = formula(max(max(Plan.instances.chance), 0))  @plan_test
        "Chance that the best plan meets its plan"
    readonly best_length: formula(days) = formula(max(max(Plan.instances.best_term), 0 days))  @plan_test
        "Length of the best plan"
    status ok when this.doctrine == FORMED
        "Plans count on cyber attacks"
    status degraded when this.doctrine == LAPSED
        "Plans stopped counting on cyber attacks"
    status inactive
        "Plans do not count on cyber attacks"
    war_begins = event():  @wartime
        "The country goes to war: moments to use its attacks come often, and the planners review every
            quarter."
        when this.war and t >= this.war_start:
            this.war_begins.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            this.tempo = WAR
            this.next_review = t + this.war_review_interval
    review = event():  @doctrine_time
        outcome: enum[MET, MISSED] = MET
        when t >= this.next_review:
            this.review.start()
        after 0 h:
            outcome = MET if this.best_chance >= this.acceptance else MISSED
            switch outcome:
                MET:
                    "The planners find that a plan of cyber attacks meets its plan often enough."
                    this.passes_in_a_row += 1
                    this.misses_in_a_row = 0
                    this.next_review += this.war_review_interval if this.tempo == WAR else this.review_interval
                MISSED:
                    "The planners find that every plan of cyber attacks misses too often."
                    this.passes_in_a_row = 0
                    this.misses_in_a_row += 1
                    this.next_review += this.war_review_interval if this.tempo == WAR else this.review_interval
    forms = event():  @doctrine_time
        "Military plans start to count on cyber attacks."
        when not this.doctrine == FORMED and this.passes_in_a_row >= this.passes_needed:
            this.forms.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.doctrine = FORMED
            this.formed_length = this.best_length
    lapses = event():  @doctrine_lapse
        "Military plans stop counting on cyber attacks."
        when this.doctrine == FORMED and this.misses_in_a_row >= this.misses_needed:
            this.lapses.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.doctrine = LAPSED

Plan:  @plan_test
    "A plan of one length that counts on the cyber attacks that the force can mass on one objective."
    role military_planners
    input length: days = 30 days in [1 days, 91 days]  @plan_lengths
        "Length of the plan"
    readonly finished: formula(operations) = formula(effects_program.ready_rate * effect_pool.attack_served
        * this.length)  @held_capabilities @capability_pool
        "Attacks that the force finishes in the plan's time and that the pools can equip"
    readonly attacks: formula(ratio) = formula(max(military_planners.objective_share
        * (effects_program.held_ready + this.finished) / (1 operations),
        1))  @held_capabilities @objective_share
        "Attacks of the plan: those that the force holds ready and finishes in the plan's time, for the
            objective"
    readonly size: formula(ratio) = formula(max((effects_program.held_targets + this.finished
        * effects_program.positioned_size) / max(effects_program.held_ready + this.finished,
        0.001 operations) / (1 targets/operation), 1))  @held_capabilities @objective_share
        "Targets of one attack of the plan, on average"
    readonly target_mass: formula(ratio) = formula(max(military_planners.objective_share
        * (effects_program.held_targets + this.finished * effects_program.positioned_size) / (1 targets),
        1))  @plan_spread
        "Targets of the plan"
    readonly spread_mass: formula(ratio) = formula(military_planners.objective_share
        * (effects_program.held_spread + this.finished * effects_program.positioned_size
        * effects_program.made_spread) / (1 targets))  @plan_spread
        "Targets of the plan, each attack's weighted by the correlation of its targets"
    readonly depth: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.concentration_now * effects_program.types_now
        / ((1 + effects_program.diversity * max(this.size - 1, 0))
        * (1 capabilities/operation)))  @shared_depth
        "Share of the plan's effect that a failed shared capability takes"
    readonly failure: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - (1 - defenders.shared_failure)
        * exp(-defenders.failure_rate * this.length))  @shared_failure
        "Chance that one capability that today's attacks of a plan share fails in the plan's time"
    readonly failures: formula(ratio) = formula((1 + effects_program.diversity * max(this.size - 1,
        0)) * (1 capabilities/operation) / effects_program.types_now * -ln(1 - this.failure))  @shared_failure
        "Expected number of the plan's shared capabilities that fail: each kind of target system needs its
            own, and each fails with today's chance"
    readonly luck: formula(ratio) = formula((1 - effects_program.success) / effects_program.success
        * max(this.spread_mass, this.target_mass) / this.target_mass ** 2)  @plan_spread
        "Spread of the share of targets hit from the luck of each target, squared"
    readonly common: formula(ratio) = formula((1 - effects_program.success) ** 2
        * defenders.common_spread ** 2)  @plan_spread
        "Spread of the share of targets hit from a cause that all targets share, squared"
    readonly attack_spread: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt(this.luck + this.common))  @plan_spread
        "Spread of the share of targets that the plan's attacks hit, as a share of its mean"
    readonly spread: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt(this.attack_spread ** 2
        + military_planners.plan_error ** 2))  @plan_spread
        "Spread of the share of targets hit around the planned share, as a share of it"
    readonly held: formula(fraction) = formula(erf(military_planners.tolerance / (sqrt(2) * this.spread))
        if military_planners.two_sided else (1 + erf(military_planners.tolerance / (sqrt(2) * this.spread)))
        / 2)  @plan_spread
        "Chance of meeting the plan when no shared capability fails"
    readonly loss_1: formula(fraction) = formula(min(this.depth, 1))  @shared_failure
        "Share of the plan's effect that one failed shared capability takes"
    readonly loss_2: formula(fraction) = formula(min(2 * this.depth, 1))  @shared_failure
        "Share that two failed shared capabilities take"
    readonly loss_3: formula(fraction) = formula(min(3 * this.depth, 1))  @shared_failure
        "Share that three failed shared capabilities take"
    readonly none_fail: formula(fraction) = formula(exp(-this.failures))  @shared_failure
        "Chance that no shared capability fails: the failures are independent, so their count is Poisson"
    readonly two_or_more: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - this.none_fail * (1
        + this.failures))  @shared_failure
        "Chance that two or more shared capabilities fail"
    readonly three_or_more: formula(fraction) = formula(this.two_or_more - this.none_fail * this.failures ** 2
        / 2)  @shared_failure
        "Chance that three or more fail"
    readonly four_or_more: formula(fraction) = formula(this.three_or_more - this.none_fail
        * this.failures ** 3 / 6)  @shared_failure
        "Chance that four or more fail"
    readonly tail_count: formula(ratio) = formula(clip(this.failures * this.three_or_more / this.four_or_more,
        4, 1000) if this.four_or_more > 1e-12 else 4)  @shared_failure
        "Mean number of failed shared capabilities when four or more fail"
    readonly tail_spread: formula(ratio) = formula(max((this.failures ** 2 * this.two_or_more + this.failures
        * this.three_or_more) / this.four_or_more - this.tail_count ** 2, 0) if this.four_or_more > 1e-12
        else 0)  @shared_failure
        "Variance of that number"
    readonly loss_4: formula(fraction) = formula(clip(this.tail_count * this.depth, min(4 * this.depth, 1),
        1))  @shared_failure
        "Share that four or more failed shared capabilities take, at their mean number"
    readonly spread_1: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt((1 - this.loss_1) * this.luck + (1 - this.loss_1) ** 2
        * this.common + military_planners.plan_error ** 2))  @shared_failure
        "Spread of the share of targets hit when one shared capability fails: the luck of the attacks left"
    readonly spread_2: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt((1 - this.loss_2) * this.luck + (1 - this.loss_2) ** 2
        * this.common + military_planners.plan_error ** 2))  @shared_failure
        "The same spread when two fail"
    readonly spread_3: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt((1 - this.loss_3) * this.luck + (1 - this.loss_3) ** 2
        * this.common + military_planners.plan_error ** 2))  @shared_failure
        "The same spread when three fail"
    readonly spread_4: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt((1 - this.loss_4) * this.luck + (1 - this.loss_4) ** 2
        * this.common + military_planners.plan_error ** 2 + (this.depth ** 2 * this.tail_spread
        if this.tail_count * this.depth < 1 else 0)))  @shared_failure
        "The same spread when four or more fail, with the spread of their number while they take less than the
            whole plan"
    readonly held_1: formula(fraction) = formula((erf((this.loss_1 + military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_1)) - erf((this.loss_1 - military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2) * this.spread_1))) / 2
        if military_planners.two_sided else (1 + erf((military_planners.tolerance - this.loss_1) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_1))) / 2)  @shared_failure
        "Chance of meeting the plan when one shared capability fails"
    readonly held_2: formula(fraction) = formula((erf((this.loss_2 + military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_2)) - erf((this.loss_2 - military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2) * this.spread_2))) / 2
        if military_planners.two_sided else (1 + erf((military_planners.tolerance - this.loss_2) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_2))) / 2)  @shared_failure
        "Chance of meeting the plan when two fail"
    readonly held_3: formula(fraction) = formula((erf((this.loss_3 + military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_3)) - erf((this.loss_3 - military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2) * this.spread_3))) / 2
        if military_planners.two_sided else (1 + erf((military_planners.tolerance - this.loss_3) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_3))) / 2)  @shared_failure
        "Chance of meeting the plan when three fail"
    readonly held_4: formula(fraction) = formula((erf((this.loss_4 + military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_4)) - erf((this.loss_4 - military_planners.tolerance) / (sqrt(2) * this.spread_4))) / 2
        if military_planners.two_sided else (1 + erf((military_planners.tolerance - this.loss_4) / (sqrt(2)
        * this.spread_4))) / 2)  @shared_failure
        "Chance of meeting the plan when four or more fail"
    readonly chance: formula(fraction) = formula(this.none_fail * (this.held + this.failures * this.held_1
        + this.failures ** 2 / 2 * this.held_2 + this.failures ** 3 / 6 * this.held_3) + this.four_or_more
        * this.held_4)  @plan_test
        "Chance that the plan's attacks hit their planned share of targets, within the tolerance: the mean
            over the number of shared capabilities that fail"
    readonly best_term: formula(days) = formula(this.length if this.chance >= military_planners.best_chance
        else 0 days)  @plan_test
        "The plan's length if it is the best plan, else zero"

day_plan: Plan
    "A plan of one day: a salvo that opens an operation."
    length = 1 days  @plan_lengths

week_plan: Plan
    "A plan of one week."
    length = 7 days  @plan_lengths

month_plan: Plan
    "A plan of one month: a campaign."

quarter_plan: Plan
    "A plan of one quarter: a long campaign."
    length = 91 days  @plan_lengths

effects_program:  @program_basis
    "The country's cyber force when it makes attacks: its experts, its access and its tools. An AI agent does
        more of the work as AI improves."
    title "Effects program"
    role adversary
    input actor = "The AI"
    input supervision: ratio = 0.2 in [0.05, 0.5]  @stage_supervision
        "Expert work to supervise AI work, for each unit of it, when one expert runs one attack at a time"
    input parallel_now: ratio = 1 in [1, 3]  @stage_supervision
        "Attacks that one expert supervises at once today"
    input parallel_end: ratio = 10 in [1, 50]  @stage_supervision
        "Attacks that one expert supervises at once at the end of AI progress"
    input compute_now: USD2025_m/person/year = 0.1 USD2025_m/person/year in [0.02 USD2025_m/person/year,
        2 USD2025_m/person/year]  @stage_compute
        "Cost of the compute for AI work today, per expert-year of the work that it replaces"
    input compute_end: USD2025_m/person/year = 0.01 USD2025_m/person/year in [0.001 USD2025_m/person/year,
        0.4 USD2025_m/person/year]  @stage_compute
        "Cost of the compute for AI work at the end of AI progress"
    input warning_time: years = 0.1 years in [0.02 years, 0.5 years]  @waiting_cost
        "Time from the decision to attack until the attack must land"
    input waiting_sharpness: ratio = 2 in [1, 4]  @waiting_cost
        "Sharpness of the change from attacks built on demand to attacks built in advance"
    input access_decay: per_year = 0.3 per_year in [0.1 per_year, 1 per_year]  @access_decay
        "Rate at which access built in advance is lost to patches and changes"
    input upkeep: per_year = 0.2 per_year in [0.05 per_year, 0.5 per_year]  @waiting_cost
        "Work each year to keep access built in advance, as a share of its build"
    input use_rate: per_year = 0.5 per_year in [0.1 per_year, 2 per_year]  @waiting_cost
        "Rate at which a moment to use an attack built in advance comes"
    input cost_learning: fraction = 0.3 in [0, 0.6]  @cost_learning
        "Share of the work of an attack that all lessons save"
    input exposure: fraction = 0.25 in [0.02, 0.99]  @exposure_basis
        "Chance that an attack exposes its access and tools when the country uses it"
    input spy_source: fraction = 0.1 in [0, 0.5]  @capability_sources
        "Share of an attack's zero-days today that surveillance already uses"
    input reuse_source: fraction = 0.05 in [0, 0.15]  @capability_sources
        "Share of an attack's zero-days today that an earlier attack used and did not burn"
    input initial_share: fraction = 0.5 in [0.1, 0.9]  @access_split
        "Share of the time and the work of access that initial access takes: movement inside the network takes
            the rest"
    input concentration_now: fraction = 0.5 in [0.2, 0.9]  @plan_concentration
        "Share of a plan's effect today that depends on one capability that its attacks share"
    input diversity: fraction = 0.1 in [0, 1]  @target_kinds
        "Chance that a further target of an attack runs a kind of system that its other targets do not"
    input tailoring_end: fraction = 0.8 in [0, 1]  @tailoring
        "Share of the steps that the targets of an attack share that AI tailors to each target at the end"
    input targets_now: targets/operation = 1 targets/operation in [1 targets/operation,
        3 targets/operation]  @targets_basis
        "Targets of one attack today"
    input targets_end: targets/operation = 30 targets/operation in [1 targets/operation,
        100 targets/operation]  @targets_basis
        "Targets of one attack at the end of AI progress"
    input success_now: fraction = 0.2 in [0.05, 0.4]  @success_basis
        "Chance today that an attack gives its intended effect on one target"
    input success_best: fraction = 0.7 in [0.4, 0.95]  @success_basis
        "Chance with every lesson learned"
    input value_scale: ratio = 1 in [0.25, 4]  @value_scale
        "Value of an effect as a multiple of the value that today's split shows"
    input saturation: targets/year = 1000 targets/year in [100 targets/year,
        10000 targets/year]  @diminishing_value
        "Targets hit in a year at which each effect is worth half as much"
    input value_learning: ratio = 1 in [0, 3]  @value_learning
        "Extra value of each effect with every lesson learned"
    readonly value_learning_log: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(1 + this.value_learning))  @value_learning
        "Logarithm of the growth of the value of each effect with every lesson learned"
    input risk_aversion: ratio = 0 in [0, 4]  @risk_value
        "Aversion of the leaders to the spread of the yearly value of attacks"
    input assessment_reliability: fraction = 0.4 in [0.2, 0.6]  @assessment_basis
        "Share of what one outcome teaches that the damage assessment keeps"
    input assessment_noise: ratio = 0.8 in [0.3, 2]  @assessment_noise
        "Error of the damage assessment of one outcome, in log units"
    input common_error: ratio = 0.3 in [0, 1]  @assessment_common
        "Error of a yearly assessment that all of its outcomes share, in log units"
    input assessment_bias_change: ratio = 0 in [-0.5, 0.5]  @assessment_bias
        "Change of the bias of the assessment at the end of AI progress, in log units"
    input access_learning: fraction = 0.1 in [0, 0.3]  @access_lessons
        "Share of the work of access that each doubling of the lessons of access saves"
    input access_forget_rate: per_year = 0.2 per_year in [0.05 per_year, 0.5 per_year]  @access_lessons
        "Rate at which the force loses its lessons of access"
    input task_overlap: fraction = 0.7 in [0.3, 1]  @access_lessons
        "Share of surveillance's work to build an access that teaches the access of an attack"
    input war_use_rate: per_year = 12 per_year in [2 per_year, 52 per_year]  @wartime
        "Rate at which the moment to use an attack held ready comes in war"
    input war_warning_time: years = 0.02 years in [0.005 years, 0.1 years]  @wartime
        "Time from the decision to attack until the attack must land, in war"
    input prior_strength: targets = 5000 targets in [300 targets, 20000 targets]  @learning_curve
        "Assessed outcomes at which lessons have half of the weight in the force's choices"
    input curve_shape: ratio = 1 in [1, 3]  @learning_curve
        "Shape of the learning curve: 1 for the Bayesian weight of the evidence"
    input exponential_curve: bool = false  @learning_forms
        "Lessons follow an exponential curve"
    input forget_rate: per_year = 0.3 per_year in [0.1 per_year, 0.7 per_year]  @forgetting
        "Rate at which the force loses its lessons"
    input burn_share: fraction = 0 in [0, 0.8]  @burned_lessons
        "Share of today's loss of lessons that comes from exposed attacks"
    readonly parallel: formula(ratio) = formula(this.parallel_now * exp(ai_tools.progress
        * ln(this.parallel_end / this.parallel_now)))  @stage_supervision
        "Attacks that one expert supervises at once"
    readonly compute: formula(USD2025_m/person/year) = formula(this.compute_now * exp(ai_tools.progress
        * ln(this.compute_end / this.compute_now)))  @stage_compute
        "Cost of the compute for AI work, per expert-year of the work that it replaces"
    readonly automation: formula(fraction) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.ai_work)
        / sum(Stage.instances.hand_work))  @stage_ai
        "Share of the work of an attack that AI does"
    readonly lead_time: formula(years) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.lead_term))  @lead_time
        "Time to build the access and the effect of one attack"
    readonly lead_now: formula(years) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.lead_term_now))  @lead_time
        "The same time today"
    readonly cost_now: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.cost_now))  @cost_today
        "Expert work for one attack today"
    readonly operator_cost_now: formula(person
        * years/operation) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.operator_cost_now))  @expert_pools
        "Operators' work for one attack today"
    readonly compute_spending: formula(USD2025_bn/yr) = formula(this.starts * sum(Stage.instances.ai_work)
        * this.compute)  @stage_compute
        "Spending on the compute of AI work in a year"
    readonly attack_targets: formula(targets/operation) = formula(this.targets_now * exp(ai_tools.progress
        * ln(this.targets_end / this.targets_now)))  @targets_basis
        "Targets of one attack"
    readonly initial_time: formula(years) = formula(this.initial_share * access_stage.time)  @access_split
        "Time to gain initial access to a target"
    readonly initial_time_now: formula(years) = formula(this.initial_share
        * access_stage.time_now)  @access_split
        "The same time today"
    readonly movement_time: formula(years) = formula((1 - this.initial_share)
        * access_stage.time)  @access_split
        "Time to move inside a target's network to the systems that the effect needs"
    readonly movement_time_now: formula(years) = formula((1 - this.initial_share)
        * access_stage.time_now)  @access_split
        "The same time today"
    readonly initial_work: formula(person * years/target) = formula(this.initial_share
        * access_stage.learned_cost / this.attack_targets)  @access_split
        "Operators' work to gain initial access to one target"
    readonly movement_work: formula(person * years/target) = formula((1 - this.initial_share)
        * access_stage.learned_cost / this.attack_targets)  @access_split
        "Operators' work to move inside one target's network"
    readonly built_ahead: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - 1 / (1 + exp(this.waiting_sharpness
        * ln(this.lead_time / this.warning))))  @waiting_cost
        "Share of attacks that need access built in advance"
    readonly built_ahead_now: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - 1 / (1 + exp(this.waiting_sharpness
        * ln(this.lead_now / this.warning_time))))  @waiting_cost
        "Share of attacks today that need access built in advance"
    readonly moment_rate: formula(per_year) = formula(this.war_use_rate if military_planners.tempo == WAR
        else this.use_rate)  @wartime
        "Rate at which the moment to use an attack held ready comes"
    readonly warning: formula(years) = formula(this.war_warning_time if military_planners.tempo == WAR
        else this.warning_time)  @wartime
        "Time from the decision to attack until the attack must land"
    readonly waiting: formula(ratio) = formula(1 + this.built_ahead * (this.access_decay + this.upkeep)
        / this.moment_rate)  @waiting_cost
        "Work of an attack with the cost of waiting, as a multiple of its build"
    readonly waiting_now: formula(ratio) = formula(1 + this.built_ahead_now * (this.access_decay
        + this.upkeep) / this.use_rate)  @waiting_cost
        "The same multiple today"
    readonly base_cost: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.cost))  @stage_cost
        "Expert work for one attack, before lessons"
    readonly attacks_now: formula(operations/year) = formula(leadership.share_now * leadership.experts
        / this.cost_now)  @attack_count
        "Attacks in a year today: today's experts on attacks over the work of one attack"
    readonly analyst_work_now: formula(people) = formula(this.attacks_now
        * sum(Stage.instances.analyst_cost_now))  @expert_pools
        "Analysts on attacks today"
    readonly target_count: formula(ratio) = formula(this.attack_targets
        / (1 targets/operation))  @targets_basis
        "Targets of one attack, as a number"
    readonly types: formula(capabilities/operation) = formula((1 + this.diversity * max(this.target_count - 1,
        0)) * (1 capabilities/operation))  @target_kinds
        "Kinds of target system in one attack: each needs its own capability at a step that no known flaw
            serves"
    readonly types_now: formula(capabilities/operation) = formula((1 + this.diversity * max(this.targets_now
        / (1 targets/operation) - 1, 0)) * (1 capabilities/operation))  @target_kinds
        "The same kinds today"
    readonly shared_chance_now: formula(fraction) = formula(this.success_now / (this.success_now
        + defenders.within_now * (1 - this.success_now)))  @outcome_correlation
        "Chance today that the steps that the targets of an attack share work"
    readonly shared_part_now: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(this.shared_chance_now)
        / ln(this.success_now))  @outcome_correlation
        "Share of the log-chance of success today that lies in the steps that the targets of an attack share"
    readonly tailoring: formula(fraction) = formula(this.tailoring_end * ai_tools.progress)  @tailoring
        "Share of those steps that AI tailors to each target"
    readonly shared_chance: formula(fraction) = formula(exp((1 - this.tailoring) * this.shared_part_now
        * ln(this.success_now)))  @outcome_correlation
        "Chance that the steps that the targets of an attack share work, at today's chance of success"
    readonly within_correlation: formula(fraction) = formula(this.success_now * (1 - this.shared_chance)
        / (this.shared_chance * (1 - this.success_now)))  @outcome_correlation
        "Correlation of the outcomes on the targets of one attack"
    readonly target_spread: formula(ratio) = formula(1 + (this.target_count - 1)
        * this.within_correlation)  @outcome_correlation
        "Growth of the spread of one attack's outcomes from the correlation of its targets"
    readonly independent_outcomes: formula(targets/operation) = formula(this.attack_targets
        / this.target_spread)  @outcome_correlation
        "Independent outcomes of one attack"
    readonly lessons_now: formula(targets) = formula(this.assessment_reliability * this.attacks_now
        * this.targets_now / (1 + (this.targets_now / (1 targets/operation) - 1) * defenders.within_now)
        / this.forget_rate)  @lessons_today
        "Lessons that the force keeps today"
    readonly weight_ratio: formula(ratio) = formula(this.know_how / this.prior_strength)  @learning_curve
        "Lessons as a multiple of the prior strength"
    readonly ratio_now: formula(ratio) = formula(this.lessons_now / this.prior_strength)  @learning_curve
        "The same multiple today"
    readonly curve_power: formula(ratio) = formula(exp(this.curve_shape
        * ln(this.weight_ratio)))  @learning_curve
        "Lessons over the prior strength, to the power of the curve's shape"
    readonly curve_power_now: formula(ratio) = formula(exp(this.curve_shape
        * ln(this.ratio_now)))  @learning_curve
        "The same power today"
    readonly weight: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - exp(-this.weight_ratio * this.ln_two)
        if this.exponential_curve else 1 - 1 / (1 + this.curve_power))  @learning_forms
        "Weight of lessons in the force's choices"
    readonly ln_two: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(2))  @learning_forms
        "Natural logarithm of 2"
    # The gain is the weight's change since today over what was left to learn today: (k - k0) / (1 - k0).
    # Each form writes it without the division, so the domain proof holds for every input.
    readonly gain: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - exp(clip((this.ratio_now - this.weight_ratio) * this.ln_two,
        -700, 700)) if this.exponential_curve else 1 - (1 + this.curve_power_now) / (1
        + this.curve_power))  @learning_curve
        "Gain of the lessons since today, as a share of what was left to learn"
    readonly cost: formula(person
        * years/operation) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.learned_cost))  @cost_learning
        "Expert work for one attack"
    readonly operator_cost: formula(person
        * years/operation) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.operator_cost))  @expert_pools
        "Operators' work for one attack"
    readonly effects_base: formula(person
        * years/operation) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.effects_cost))  @cost_learning
        "Operators' work of an attack in the stages that only attacks do, before lessons"
    readonly effects_share_now: formula(fraction) = formula(sum(Stage.instances.effects_cost_now)
        / this.operator_cost_now)  @cost_learning
        "Share of today's work of the operators for an attack in the stages that only attacks do"
    readonly wanted_starts: formula(operations/year) = formula(leadership.attack_experts
        / this.operator_cost)  @attack_count
        "Attacks that the operators on attacks can start in a year"
    # The analysts on attacks assess the damage of the attacks made first, then plan new ones.
    readonly assessment_part: formula(fraction) = formula(this.assessing / assessment_stage.time
        * assessment_stage.learned_cost / max(this.assessing / assessment_stage.time
        * assessment_stage.learned_cost + this.wanted_starts * planning_stage.learned_cost,
        0.001 people))  @analyst_split
        "Share of the analysts' hours on attacks that damage assessment may take: its share of the work
            waiting"
    readonly assessed_rate: formula(operations/year) = formula(min(this.assessing / assessment_stage.time,
        analysts.attack_capacity * this.assessment_part
        / assessment_stage.learned_cost))  @assessment_time @analyst_split
        "Attacks whose damage assessment ends in a year"
    readonly planning_left: formula(people) = formula(max(analysts.attack_capacity - this.assessed_rate
        * assessment_stage.learned_cost, 0 people))  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work on attacks that is left for planning after damage assessment"
    readonly supply: formula(fraction) = formula(access_pool.attack_served * movement_pool.attack_served
        * effect_pool.attack_served)  @capability_pool
        "Share of the attacks that the pools can equip now"
    readonly starts: formula(operations/year) = formula(min(this.wanted_starts,
        this.planning_left / planning_stage.learned_cost) * this.supply)  @attack_count
        "Attacks that the force starts in a year: those that its operators can start and its analysts plan"
    readonly analysis_asked: formula(people) = formula(this.assessing / assessment_stage.time
        * assessment_stage.learned_cost + this.wanted_starts * planning_stage.learned_cost)  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work that attacks have waiting in a year: damage assessment and the planning of new attacks"
    readonly analysis_need: formula(people) = formula(max(this.assessing / assessment_stage.time,
        this.wanted_starts) * assessment_stage.learned_cost + this.wanted_starts
        * planning_stage.learned_cost)  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work that the attacks the operators can start need in a year, or the queue if it is larger"
    readonly analysis_done: formula(people) = formula(this.assessed_rate * assessment_stage.learned_cost
        + this.starts * planning_stage.learned_cost)  @analyst_split
        "Analysis work on attacks that the analysts do in a year"
    # The operators' hours go to the attacks farthest along first: execution, then the effect, then access.
    readonly execution_asked: formula(operations/year) = formula(this.moment_rate * this.held_ready + (1
        - this.built_ahead) * this.positioned_attacks / payload_stage.time)  @operator_priority
        "Attacks that wait for execution in a year: those held ready whose moment comes, and those built on
            demand"
    readonly executed_size: formula(targets/operation) = formula(max((this.moment_rate * this.held_targets
        + (1 - this.built_ahead) * this.positioned / payload_stage.time) / max(this.execution_asked,
        0.001 operations/year), 1 targets/operation))  @operator_priority
        "Targets of one attack that waits for execution, on average: each keeps the targets that it was built
            with"
    readonly execution_work: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((execution_stage.work
        * execution_stage.unit_cost + execution_stage.target_work * this.executed_size
        * execution_stage.target_cost) * execution_stage.learning)  @operator_priority
        "Operators' work to execute one attack that waits for execution, after lessons"
    readonly execution_served: formula(fraction) = formula(min(1, leadership.attack_experts
        / max(this.execution_asked * this.execution_work, 0.001 people)))  @operator_priority
        "Share of those attacks that the operators' hours let the force execute"
    readonly effect_hours: formula(people) = formula(max(leadership.attack_experts - this.execution_served
        * this.execution_asked * this.execution_work, 0 people))  @operator_priority
        "Operators' hours left for the effect after execution"
    readonly ready_rate: formula(operations/year) = formula(min(this.positioned_attacks / payload_stage.time,
        this.effect_hours / this.effect_work))  @attack_pipeline @operator_priority
        "Attacks whose effect the force finishes in a year: each takes the targets of one attack"
    readonly movement_hours: formula(people) = formula(max(this.effect_hours - (this.built_ahead + (1
        - this.built_ahead) * this.execution_served) * this.ready_rate * this.effect_work,
        0 people))  @operator_priority
        "Operators' hours left for movement inside the network after the effect"
    readonly movement_rate: formula(targets/year) = formula(min(this.accesses / this.movement_time,
        this.movement_hours / this.movement_work))  @attack_pipeline @operator_priority
        "Targets where the force finishes its movement inside the network in a year"
    readonly access_hours: formula(people) = formula(max(this.movement_hours - this.movement_rate
        * this.movement_work, 0 people))  @operator_priority
        "Operators' hours left for initial access after movement"
    readonly access_rate: formula(targets/year) = formula(min(this.in_access / this.initial_time,
        this.access_hours / this.initial_work))  @attack_pipeline @operator_priority
        "Targets where the force gains initial access in a year"
    readonly hold_rate: formula(operations/year) = formula(this.built_ahead
        * this.ready_rate)  @held_capabilities
        "Attacks built in advance in a year, which wait ready for their moment"
    readonly now_rate: formula(operations/year) = formula((1 - this.built_ahead) * this.ready_rate
        * this.execution_served)  @attack_pipeline @operator_priority
        "Attacks built on demand in a year, which the force makes as soon as they are ready"
    readonly attacks: formula(operations/year) = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_served
        + this.moment_rate * this.held_ready * this.execution_served)  @attack_pipeline
        "Attacks that the force makes in a year"
    readonly in_access_size: formula(targets/operation) = formula(max(this.in_access
        / max(this.in_access_attacks, 0.001 operations), 1 targets/operation))  @attack_pipeline
        "Targets of one attack in initial access, on average"
    readonly access_size: formula(targets/operation) = formula(max(this.accesses / max(this.access_attacks,
        0.001 operations), 1 targets/operation))  @attack_pipeline
        "Targets of one attack in movement, on average"
    readonly positioned_size: formula(targets/operation) = formula(max(this.positioned
        / max(this.positioned_attacks, 0.001 operations), 1 targets/operation))  @attack_pipeline
        "Targets of one attack whose effect the force builds, on average"
    readonly positioned_types: formula(capabilities/operation) = formula((1 + this.diversity
        * max(this.positioned_size / (1 targets/operation) - 1, 0))
        * (1 capabilities/operation))  @target_kinds
        "Kinds of target system of one attack whose effect the force builds"
    readonly access_target_need: formula(capabilities/target) = formula((1 + this.diversity
        * max(this.in_access_size / (1 targets/operation) - 1, 0)) * (1 capabilities/operation)
        / this.in_access_size)  @capability_use
        "Capabilities that one target in initial access needs: one for each kind of system of its attack"
    readonly movement_target_need: formula(capabilities/target) = formula((1 + this.diversity
        * max(this.access_size / (1 targets/operation) - 1, 0)) * (1 capabilities/operation)
        / this.access_size)  @capability_use
        "Capabilities that one target in movement needs: one for each kind of system of its attack"
    readonly effect_work: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((payload_stage.work
        * payload_stage.unit_cost + payload_stage.target_work * this.positioned_size
        * payload_stage.target_cost) * this.waiting * payload_stage.learning)  @operator_priority
        "Operators' work to build the effect of one attack whose effect the force builds"
    readonly made_spread: formula(ratio) = formula(1 + (this.positioned_size / (1 targets/operation) - 1)
        * this.within_correlation)  @outcome_correlation
        "Growth of the spread of the outcomes of an attack whose effect the force finishes now"
    readonly held_size: formula(targets/operation) = formula(max(this.held_targets / max(this.held_ready,
        0.001 operations), 1 targets/operation))  @held_capabilities
        "Targets of one attack held ready, on average"
    readonly assessed_size: formula(targets/operation) = formula(max(this.assessing_targets
        / max(this.assessing, 0.001 operations), 1 targets/operation))  @assessment_time
        "Targets of one attack under assessment, on average"
    readonly made_targets: formula(targets/year) = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_served
        * this.positioned_size + this.moment_rate * this.held_targets
        * this.execution_served)  @attack_pipeline
        "Targets of the attacks that the force makes in a year"
    readonly odds_now: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(this.success_now / (1 - this.success_now)))  @success_basis
        "Log-odds of success today"
    readonly odds_best: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(this.success_best / (1
        - this.success_best)))  @success_basis
        "Log-odds of success with every lesson learned"
    readonly odds: formula(ratio) = formula(this.odds_now + (this.odds_best - this.odds_now) * this.gain
        - (defenders.alertness - defenders.alert_now) - defenders.hardening)  @success_basis
        "Log-odds of success on one target"
    readonly success: formula(fraction) = formula(1 / (1 + exp(-clip(this.odds, -40, 40))))  @success_basis
        "Chance that an attack gives its intended effect on one target"
    readonly hits: formula(targets/year) = formula(this.made_targets * this.success)  @value_basis
        "Targets hit in a year"
    readonly doctrine_factor: formula(ratio) = formula(1 + military_planners.doctrine_value * (1
        if military_planners.doctrine == FORMED else 0))  @doctrine_feedback
        "Growth of the value of effects once plans count on them"
    # The calibration solves today's equal returns for the value of one effect. With foresight, the
    # assessed return counts the value of lessons, which is linear in the value of one effect, so the
    # solution stays in closed form.
    readonly effect_value_now: formula(sev/target) = formula((leadership.attack_experts_now
        * surveillance_program.spying_return_now + this.attack_cost_now + leadership.foresight
        * this.cost_slope_now * this.lesson_weight_now) / (this.hits_now / (1 + this.hits_now
        / this.saturation) * this.risk_factor_now + leadership.foresight * this.value_growth_now
        * this.lesson_weight_now))  @revealed_split
        "Value of one intended effect that today's split shows"
    readonly gain_slope_now: formula(per_target) = formula(this.ln_two / this.prior_strength
        if this.exponential_curve else this.curve_shape * this.curve_power_now / this.ratio_now / (1
        + this.curve_power_now) / this.prior_strength)  @lesson_value
        "Growth of the gain with one more lesson today"
    readonly lesson_weight_now: formula(ratio) = formula(this.lessons_now * this.forget_rate
        * this.gain_slope_now / (leadership.discount_rate + this.forget_rate))  @lesson_value
        "Discounted gain of the lessons that today's attacks teach in one year"
    readonly value_growth_now: formula(targets/year) = formula((this.hits_now * (this.cost_learning
        * this.effects_share_now + (1 - this.success_now) * (this.odds_best - this.odds_now)) / (1
        + this.hits_now / this.saturation) + this.hits_now * this.value_learning_log) / (1 + this.hits_now
        / this.saturation))  @lesson_value
        "Growth of today's counted hits in a year with the gain"
    readonly cost_slope_now: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.attacks_now * this.cost_learning
        * this.effects_share_now * (other_states.attribution_now * other_states.sanction_cost * (1 + 2
        * other_states.escalation * this.attacks_now * other_states.attribution_now)
        + this.burned_now))  @lesson_value
        "Growth of today's yearly costs of attacks with the gain"
    readonly hits_now: formula(targets/year) = formula(this.attacks_now * this.targets_now
        * this.success_now)  @value_basis
        "Targets hit in a year today"
    readonly attack_cost_now: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.attacks_now * (other_states.attribution_now
        * other_states.sanction_cost * (1 + other_states.escalation * this.attacks_now
        * other_states.attribution_now) + this.burned_now))  @politics_basis
        "Value lost to sanctions and burned access in a year today"
    readonly attack_value: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.value_scale * this.effect_value_now * this.hits
        / (1 + this.hits / this.saturation) * exp(clip(this.value_learning_log * this.gain, -700,
        700)) * this.doctrine_factor)  @value_basis
        "Value of the attacks in a year"
    readonly yearly_targets: formula(ratio) = formula(this.made_targets * (1 years)
        / (1 targets))  @value_basis
        "Targets of the attacks of one year, as a number"
    readonly learning_spread: formula(fraction) = formula(this.success * (1 - this.success) / (this.know_how
        / (1 targets) + this.prior_strength / (1 targets) + 1))  @risk_value
        "Uncertainty of the chance of success, as a variance"
    readonly value_spread: formula(ratio) = formula((1 - this.success) / this.success * this.target_spread
        / (this.yearly_targets + 1) + (1 - this.success) ** 2 * defenders.common_spread ** 2
        + this.learning_spread / this.success ** 2)  @risk_value
        "Relative variance of the value of the attacks of one year"
    readonly risk_factor: formula(ratio) = formula(1 / (1 + this.risk_aversion / 2
        * this.value_spread))  @risk_value
        "Share of the value that the leaders count after the spread"
    readonly risk_factor_now: formula(ratio) = formula(1 / (1 + this.risk_aversion / 2 * ((1
        - this.success_now) / this.success_now * (1 + (this.targets_now / (1 targets/operation) - 1)
        * defenders.within_now) / (this.attacks_now * this.targets_now * (1 years) / (1 targets) + 1) + (1
        - this.success_now) ** 2 * defenders.common_spread ** 2 + (1 - this.success_now) / this.success_now
        / (this.lessons_now / (1 targets) + this.prior_strength / (1 targets) + 1))))  @risk_value
        "Share of the value that the leaders count today"
    readonly risk_value: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.attack_value * this.risk_factor)  @risk_value
        "Value of the attacks in a year that the leaders count"
    readonly sanctions: formula(sev/operation) = formula(other_states.attribution * other_states.sanction_cost
        * (1 + other_states.escalation * this.attacks * other_states.attribution))  @politics_basis
        "Cost of the sanctions and replies for one attack"
    readonly burned: formula(sev/operation) = formula(surveillance_program.burned_accesses
        * surveillance_program.life_value / max(this.attacks, 0.001 operations/year))  @capability_burn
        "Surveillance value that one attack burns: the accesses that the defenders find through the
            capabilities that it burns"
    readonly burned_now: formula(sev/operation) = formula(surveillance_program.burned_accesses_now
        * surveillance_program.life_value / this.attacks_now)  @capability_burn
        "Surveillance value that one attack burns today"
    readonly attack_cost: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.attacks * (this.sanctions
        + this.burned))  @politics_basis
        "Value lost to sanctions and burned access in a year"
    readonly forgetting: formula(per_year) = formula(this.forget_rate * (1 - this.burn_share + this.burn_share
        * this.attacks / this.attacks_now))  @burned_lessons
        "Rate at which the force loses its lessons"
    readonly learn_rate: formula(targets/year) = formula(this.assessment_reliability * this.assessed_rate
        * this.assessing_outcomes / max(this.assessing, 0.001 operations))  @learning_basis
        "Lessons that the force gains in a year"
    readonly loss_rate: formula(targets/year) = formula(this.know_how * this.forgetting)  @forgetting
        "Lessons that the force loses in a year"
    # The value of what attacks teach: the change of the yearly net value with one more lesson, held for as
    # long as lessons last and discounted, for each expert on attacks.
    readonly gain_slope: formula(per_target) = formula(this.ln_two * exp(clip((this.ratio_now
        - this.weight_ratio) * this.ln_two, -700, 700)) / this.prior_strength if this.exponential_curve
        else (1 + this.curve_power_now) * this.curve_shape * this.curve_power / this.weight_ratio / (1
        + this.curve_power) ** 2 / this.prior_strength)  @lesson_value
        "Growth of the gain with one more lesson"
    # Where the operators limit the attacks, a lesson that cuts their work lets them start more attacks; where
    # the analysts limit them, a lesson that cuts the analysts' work of planning and assessment lets them plan
    # more. The slope blends the two by the share of the attacks wanted that start. The exact slope has a kink
    # where the two limits meet, and a jump there makes the funding rule chatter, so the blend is continuous.
    readonly analysis_work: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(planning_stage.learned_cost
        + assessment_stage.learned_cost)  @lesson_value
        "Analysts' work to plan and assess one attack"
    readonly crowding: formula(ratio) = formula(min(this.starts / max(this.wanted_starts,
        0.000001 operations/year), 1))  @lesson_value
        "Share of the attacks that the operators can start that the analysts plan"
    # The slope counts the attacks that a lower cost lets the force start, which it makes once they leave the
    # pipeline: the value of a lesson is a value at rest.
    readonly attack_slope: formula(operations/year) = formula(this.wanted_starts * this.cost_learning
        * this.effects_base / this.operator_cost * this.crowding + (1 - this.crowding) * this.starts
        * this.cost_learning * (planning_stage.cost + assessment_stage.cost)
        / this.analysis_work)  @lesson_value
        "Growth of the attacks in a year with the gain"
    readonly success_slope: formula(fraction) = formula(this.success * (1 - this.success) * (this.odds_best
        - this.odds_now))  @lesson_value
        "Growth of the chance of success with the gain"
    readonly hits_slope: formula(targets/year) = formula(this.attack_targets * (this.success
        * this.attack_slope + this.attacks * this.success_slope))  @lesson_value
        "Growth of the targets hit in a year with the gain"
    readonly value_slope: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.value_scale * this.effect_value_now
        * this.doctrine_factor * exp(clip(this.value_learning_log * this.gain, -700,
        700)) * (this.hits_slope / (1 + this.hits / this.saturation) + this.hits * this.value_learning_log)
        / (1 + this.hits / this.saturation))  @lesson_value
        "Growth of the value of the attacks of a year with the gain"
    readonly cost_slope: formula(sev/year) = formula(this.attack_slope * (other_states.attribution
        * other_states.sanction_cost * (1 + 2 * other_states.escalation * this.attacks
        * other_states.attribution) + this.burned))  @lesson_value
        "Growth of the yearly costs of attacks with the gain"
    readonly lesson_value: formula(sev/person/year) = formula((this.value_slope - this.cost_slope)
        * this.gain_slope / (leadership.discount_rate + this.forgetting) * this.assessment_reliability
        * this.independent_outcomes * this.crowding / this.operator_cost)  @lesson_value
        "Value of the lessons of one operator's year on attacks"
    readonly assessment_spread: formula(ratio) = formula(sqrt((1 - this.success) / this.success
        * this.target_spread / (this.yearly_targets + 1) + this.assessment_noise ** 2 / (this.learn_rate
        * (1 years) / (1 targets) + 1) + this.common_error ** 2))  @assessment_noise
        "Spread of the error of a yearly assessment, in log units"
    readonly assessment_bias: formula(ratio) = formula(this.assessment_bias_change
        * ai_tools.progress)  @assessment_bias
        "Bias of the assessment of the value of attacks, in log units"
    know_how: targets = this.lessons_now in [1 targets,
        1000000 targets] scale 10000 targets  @learning_balance
        "Lessons that the force keeps: assessed outcomes"
    attacks_made: operations = 0 operations scale 100000 operations  @attack_count
        "Attacks made since the start"
    # The targets and the attacks on their way from start to assessment. Each stock starts at its rest value
    # today: what passes in a year today times the time in the stock.
    in_access: targets = this.attacks_now * this.targets_now * this.initial_time_now in [0 targets,
        100000000 targets] scale 100 targets  @attack_pipeline
        "Targets where the force is gaining initial access"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.access_rate)  @attack_pipeline
    accesses: targets = this.attacks_now * this.targets_now * this.movement_time_now in [0 targets,
        100000000 targets] scale 100 targets  @attack_pipeline
        "Targets where the force has access and moves inside the network"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.movement_rate)  @attack_pipeline
    positioned: targets = this.attacks_now * this.targets_now * payload_stage.time_now in [0 targets,
        100000000 targets] scale 100 targets  @attack_pipeline
        "Targets where the force sits on the systems that the effect needs, while it builds the effect"
        outflow.capacity = formula((this.hold_rate + this.now_rate) * this.positioned_size)  @attack_pipeline
    held_ready: operations = this.built_ahead_now * this.attacks_now / this.use_rate in [0 operations,
        10000000 operations] scale 1000 operations  @held_capabilities
        "Attacks built in advance that the force holds ready for their moment"
    assessing: operations = this.attacks_now * assessment_stage.time_now in [0 operations,
        10000000 operations] scale 100 operations  @assessment_time
        "Attacks made whose damage the force is assessing"
    in_access_attacks: operations = this.attacks_now * this.initial_time_now in [0 operations,
        100000000 operations] scale 100 operations  @attack_pipeline
        "Attacks whose targets the force is gaining initial access to"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.access_rate / this.in_access_size)  @attack_pipeline
    access_attacks: operations = this.attacks_now * this.movement_time_now in [0 operations,
        100000000 operations] scale 100 operations  @attack_pipeline
        "Attacks whose targets the force has access to and moves inside"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.movement_rate / this.access_size)  @attack_pipeline
    positioned_attacks: operations = this.attacks_now * payload_stage.time_now in [0 operations,
        100000000 operations] scale 100 operations  @attack_pipeline
        "Attacks whose effect the force builds"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.hold_rate + this.now_rate)  @attack_pipeline
    held_spread: targets = this.built_ahead_now * this.attacks_now * this.targets_now * (1 + (this.targets_now
        / (1 targets/operation) - 1) * defenders.within_now) / this.use_rate in [0 targets,
        1000000000 targets] scale 1000 targets  @held_capabilities @outcome_correlation
        "Targets of the attacks held ready, each attack's weighted by the correlation of its targets"
    held_outcomes: targets = this.built_ahead_now * this.attacks_now * this.targets_now / (1
        + (this.targets_now / (1 targets/operation) - 1)
        * defenders.within_now) / this.use_rate in [0 targets,
        1000000000 targets] scale 1000 targets  @held_capabilities @outcome_correlation
        "Independent outcomes of the attacks held ready"
    assessing_outcomes: targets = this.attacks_now * this.targets_now / (1 + (this.targets_now
        / (1 targets/operation) - 1) * defenders.within_now) * assessment_stage.time_now in [0 targets,
        1000000000 targets] scale 100 targets  @assessment_time @outcome_correlation
        "Independent outcomes of the attacks whose damage the force is assessing"
    held_targets: targets = this.built_ahead_now * this.attacks_now * this.targets_now / this.use_rate in [0 targets,
        1000000000 targets] scale 1000 targets  @held_capabilities
        "Targets of the attacks held ready: each keeps the targets that it was built with"
    assessing_targets: targets = this.attacks_now * this.targets_now * assessment_stage.time_now in [0 targets,
        1000000000 targets] scale 100 targets  @assessment_time
        "Targets of the attacks whose damage the force is assessing"
    flow start_build:  @attack_count
        "The force starts attacks: their targets enter initial access."
        flow in_access: SOURCE -> this.in_access
            request = formula(this.starts * this.attack_targets)
        flow in_access_attacks: SOURCE -> this.in_access_attacks
            request = formula(this.starts)
    # Each step moves in parts, one for each source of the capabilities that its targets need. A part moves
    # together with the stock that it draws on, so an empty source holds back only its own part.
    flow access_known:  @attack_pipeline @one_day_chance
        "The force gains initial access to targets through known flaws."
        flow accesses: this.in_access -> this.accesses
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.one_day)
        flow access_attacks: this.in_access_attacks -> this.access_attacks
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.one_day / this.in_access_size)
    flow access_spy:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force gains initial access to targets with capabilities that surveillance uses."
        flow accesses: this.in_access -> this.accesses
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_spy)
        flow access_attacks: this.in_access_attacks -> this.access_attacks
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_spy / this.in_access_size)
        flow access_pool_held_shared: access_pool.spy_used -> access_pool.held_shared
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_spy * this.access_target_need)
    flow access_kept_shared:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force gains initial access to targets with kept capabilities of earlier attacks that surveillance
            also uses."
        flow accesses: this.in_access -> this.accesses
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_kept_shared)
        flow access_attacks: this.in_access_attacks -> this.access_attacks
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_kept_shared / this.in_access_size)
        flow access_pool_held_shared: access_pool.kept_shared -> access_pool.held_shared
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_kept_shared
                * this.access_target_need)
    flow access_kept_attack:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force gains initial access to targets with kept capabilities of earlier attacks."
        flow accesses: this.in_access -> this.accesses
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_kept_attack)
        flow access_attacks: this.in_access_attacks -> this.access_attacks
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_kept_attack / this.in_access_size)
        flow access_pool_held_attack: access_pool.kept_attack -> access_pool.held_attack
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_kept_attack
                * this.access_target_need)
    flow access_new:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force gains initial access to targets with capabilities that no one has used."
        flow accesses: this.in_access -> this.accesses
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_new)
        flow access_attacks: this.in_access_attacks -> this.access_attacks
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_new / this.in_access_size)
        flow access_pool_held_attack: access_pool.fresh -> access_pool.held_attack
            request = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_part_new * this.access_target_need)
    flow move_known:  @attack_pipeline @one_day_chance
        "The force moves inside targets' networks through known flaws."
        flow positioned: this.accesses -> this.positioned
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.one_day)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.access_attacks -> this.positioned_attacks
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.one_day / this.access_size)
    flow move_spy:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force moves inside targets' networks with capabilities that surveillance uses."
        flow positioned: this.accesses -> this.positioned
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_spy)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.access_attacks -> this.positioned_attacks
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_spy / this.access_size)
        flow movement_pool_held_shared: movement_pool.spy_used -> movement_pool.held_shared
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_spy * this.movement_target_need)
    flow move_kept_shared:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force moves inside targets' networks with kept capabilities of earlier attacks that surveillance
            also uses."
        flow positioned: this.accesses -> this.positioned
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_kept_shared)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.access_attacks -> this.positioned_attacks
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_kept_shared / this.access_size)
        flow movement_pool_held_shared: movement_pool.kept_shared -> movement_pool.held_shared
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_kept_shared
                * this.movement_target_need)
    flow move_kept_attack:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force moves inside targets' networks with kept capabilities of earlier attacks."
        flow positioned: this.accesses -> this.positioned
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_kept_attack)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.access_attacks -> this.positioned_attacks
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_kept_attack / this.access_size)
        flow movement_pool_held_attack: movement_pool.kept_attack -> movement_pool.held_attack
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_kept_attack
                * this.movement_target_need)
    flow move_new:  @attack_pipeline @capability_use
        "The force moves inside targets' networks with capabilities that no one has used."
        flow positioned: this.accesses -> this.positioned
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_new)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.access_attacks -> this.positioned_attacks
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_new / this.access_size)
        flow movement_pool_held_attack: movement_pool.fresh -> movement_pool.held_attack
            request = formula(this.movement_rate * movement_pool.attack_part_new * this.movement_target_need)
    # The effect turns the targets of one attack into an attack, with one capability of the effect for each kind
    # of system. An attack built in advance holds its capabilities while it waits; an attack built on demand is
    # made at once, so an exposed one burns them and a hidden one keeps them.
    flow prepare_known:  @held_capabilities @one_day_chance
        "The force builds an effect in advance through known flaws."
        flow positioned: this.positioned -> SINK
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.one_day * this.positioned_size)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.positioned_attacks -> SINK
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.one_day)
        flow held_ready: SOURCE -> this.held_ready
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.one_day)
        flow held_targets: SOURCE -> this.held_targets
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.one_day * this.positioned_size)
        flow held_spread: SOURCE -> this.held_spread
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.one_day * this.positioned_size * this.made_spread)
        flow held_outcomes: SOURCE -> this.held_outcomes
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.one_day * this.positioned_size / this.made_spread)
    flow prepare_kept:  @held_capabilities @capability_use
        "The force builds an effect in advance with kept capabilities of earlier attacks."
        flow positioned: this.positioned -> SINK
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_size)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.positioned_attacks -> SINK
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack)
        flow held_ready: SOURCE -> this.held_ready
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack)
        flow held_targets: SOURCE -> this.held_targets
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_size)
        flow held_spread: SOURCE -> this.held_spread
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_size
                * this.made_spread)
        flow held_outcomes: SOURCE -> this.held_outcomes
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_size
                / this.made_spread)
        flow effect_pool_held_attack: effect_pool.kept_attack -> effect_pool.held_attack
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_types)
    flow prepare_new:  @held_capabilities @capability_use
        "The force builds an effect in advance with capabilities that no one has used."
        flow positioned: this.positioned -> SINK
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_size)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.positioned_attacks -> SINK
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new)
        flow held_ready: SOURCE -> this.held_ready
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new)
        flow held_targets: SOURCE -> this.held_targets
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_size)
        flow held_spread: SOURCE -> this.held_spread
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_size
                * this.made_spread)
        flow held_outcomes: SOURCE -> this.held_outcomes
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_size
                / this.made_spread)
        flow effect_pool_held_attack: effect_pool.fresh -> effect_pool.held_attack
            request = formula(this.hold_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_types)
    flow now_known:  @attack_pipeline @operator_priority @one_day_chance
        "The force makes an attack built on demand through known flaws as soon as it is ready."
        flow positioned: this.positioned -> SINK
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.one_day * this.positioned_size)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.positioned_attacks -> SINK
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.one_day)
        flow assessing: SOURCE -> this.assessing
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.one_day)
        flow assessing_targets: SOURCE -> this.assessing_targets
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.one_day * this.positioned_size)
        flow assessing_outcomes: SOURCE -> this.assessing_outcomes
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.one_day * this.positioned_size / this.made_spread)
    flow now_kept:  @attack_pipeline @capability_burn
        "The force makes an attack built on demand with kept capabilities as soon as it is ready."
        flow positioned: this.positioned -> SINK
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_size)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.positioned_attacks -> SINK
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack)
        flow assessing: SOURCE -> this.assessing
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack)
        flow assessing_targets: SOURCE -> this.assessing_targets
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_size)
        flow assessing_outcomes: SOURCE -> this.assessing_outcomes
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_size
                / this.made_spread)
        flow effect_pool_burned: effect_pool.kept_attack -> effect_pool.burned
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_kept_attack * this.positioned_types
                * this.exposure)
    flow now_new:  @attack_pipeline @capability_burn
        "The force makes an attack built on demand with capabilities that no one has used as soon as it is
            ready."
        flow positioned: this.positioned -> SINK
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_size)
        flow positioned_attacks: this.positioned_attacks -> SINK
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new)
        flow assessing: SOURCE -> this.assessing
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new)
        flow assessing_targets: SOURCE -> this.assessing_targets
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_size)
        flow assessing_outcomes: SOURCE -> this.assessing_outcomes
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_size
                / this.made_spread)
        flow effect_pool_burned: effect_pool.fresh -> effect_pool.burned
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_types
                * this.exposure)
        flow effect_pool_kept_attack: effect_pool.fresh -> effect_pool.kept_attack
            request = formula(this.now_rate * effect_pool.attack_part_new * this.positioned_types * (1
                - this.exposure))
    flow use_held:  @held_capabilities @operator_priority
        "The moment of an attack held ready comes, and the force makes it."
        flow assessing: this.held_ready -> this.assessing
            request = formula(this.moment_rate * this.held_ready * this.execution_served)
        flow assessing_targets: this.held_targets -> this.assessing_targets
            request = formula(this.moment_rate * this.held_targets * this.execution_served)
        flow held_spread: this.held_spread -> SINK
            request = formula(this.moment_rate * this.held_spread * this.execution_served)
        flow assessing_outcomes: this.held_outcomes -> this.assessing_outcomes
            request = formula(this.moment_rate * this.held_outcomes * this.execution_served)
    flow assessment_ends:  @assessment_time
        "The damage assessment of an attack ends, and its lessons count."
        flow assessing: this.assessing -> SINK
            request = formula(this.assessed_rate)
        flow assessing_targets: this.assessing_targets -> SINK
            request = formula(this.assessed_rate * this.assessed_size)
        flow assessing_outcomes: this.assessing_outcomes -> SINK
            request = formula(this.assessed_rate * this.assessing_outcomes / max(this.assessing,
                0.001 operations))
    readonly access_learn_rate: formula(accesses/year) = formula(this.access_rate * access_pool.attack_served
        * (1 accesses) / (1 targets) + this.task_overlap * surveillance_program.access_rate
        * access_pool.spy_served)  @access_lessons
        "Lessons of access that the force gains in a year: the accesses built for attacks, and the accesses
            that surveillance gains as far as the tasks overlap"
    readonly access_lessons_now: formula(accesses) = formula((this.attacks_now * this.targets_now
        * (1 accesses) / (1 targets) + this.task_overlap * surveillance_program.builds_now)
        / this.access_forget_rate)  @access_lessons
        "Lessons of access that the force keeps today"
    readonly access_factor: formula(ratio) = formula(exp(clip(ln(1 - this.access_learning) / this.ln_two
        * ln(this.access_know_how / this.access_lessons_now), -700, 700)))  @access_lessons
        "Work of access as a multiple of today's, from the lessons of access"
    access_know_how: accesses = this.access_lessons_now in [1 accesses,
        10000000000 accesses] scale 10000 accesses  @access_lessons
        "Lessons of access that the force keeps: accesses built"
    flow learn_access: SOURCE -> this.access_know_how  @access_lessons
        "The force learns from the accesses that it and surveillance build."
        request = formula(this.access_learn_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.access_learn_rate)
    flow forget_access: this.access_know_how -> SINK  @access_lessons
        "The force loses lessons of access to patches, turnover and the disclosure of its tools."
        request = formula(this.access_know_how * this.access_forget_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.access_know_how * this.access_forget_rate)
    flow learn: SOURCE -> this.know_how  @learning_basis
        "The force learns from the assessed outcomes of its attacks."
        request = formula(this.learn_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.learn_rate)
    flow forget: this.know_how -> SINK  @forgetting
        "The force loses lessons to patches, burned tools, staff turnover and secrecy."
        request = formula(this.loss_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.loss_rate)
    flow tally: SOURCE -> this.attacks_made  @attack_count
        "The force makes attacks."
        request = formula(this.attacks)
        capacity = formula(this.attacks)
    start = event():  @period_start
        "The period starts in 2026, with today's split of the country's cyber experts."
        when t >= 0 years:
            this.start.start()

Stage:  @stage_basis
    "A kind of work that an attack needs. AI does a growing share of it."
    role effects_program
    input work: person * years/operation = 1 person * years/operation in [0.05 person * years/operation,
        10 person * years/operation]  @stage_work
        "Expert work by hand for one attack, apart from its targets"
    input target_work: person * years/target = 0.5 person * years/target in [0 person * years/target,
        10 person * years/target]  @stage_work
        "Expert work by hand for each target of an attack"
    input ai_now: fraction = 0 in [0, 0.9]  @stage_ai
        "Share of the work that AI does today"
    input ai_end: fraction = 0.5 in [0, 0.95]  @stage_ai
        "Share of the work that AI does at the end of AI progress"
    input payload_path: bool = false  @stage_paths
        "The work moves with AI progress on payloads, which is slower than progress on access"
    input split_ai: bool = false  @stage_split
        "The work for each target has its own AI share, apart from the work for the attack"
    input target_ai_now: fraction = 0 in [0, 0.9]  @stage_split
        "Share of the work for each target that AI does today"
    input target_ai_end: fraction = 0.5 in [0, 0.9]  @stage_split
        "Share of the work for each target that AI does at the end of AI progress"
    input target_payload_path: bool = false  @stage_split
        "The work for each target moves with AI progress on payloads, which is slower than progress on access"
    input held: bool = false  @waiting_cost
        "The work's product waits ready for its use, decays and needs upkeep"
    input builds: bool = false  @lead_time
        "The work's time counts in the time to build an attack"
    input time_now: years = 0.1 years in [0.003 years, 5 years]  @lead_time
        "Time that the work takes today"
    input time_end: years = 0.1 years in [0.001 years, 5 years]  @lead_time
        "Time that the work takes at the end of AI progress"
    readonly progress: formula(fraction) = formula(ai_tools.payload_progress if this.payload_path
        else ai_tools.progress)  @stage_paths
        "AI progress that reaches the work"
    readonly ai_share: formula(fraction) = formula(this.ai_now + (this.ai_end - this.ai_now)
        * this.progress)  @stage_ai
        "Share of the work that AI does"
    readonly stage_targets: formula(targets/operation) = formula(effects_program.attack_targets)  @stage_work
        "Targets of the attacks that the work serves"
    readonly hand_work: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(this.work + this.target_work
        * this.stage_targets)  @stage_work
        "Expert work by hand for one attack with its targets"
    readonly hand_work_now: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(this.work + this.target_work
        * effects_program.targets_now)  @stage_work
        "The same work for one attack today"
    readonly overhead: formula(ratio) = formula(effects_program.supervision / effects_program.parallel
        + effects_program.compute / leadership.expert_cost)  @stage_ai
        "Cost of a unit of AI work as a share of its cost by hand: the supervision and the compute"
    readonly overhead_now: formula(ratio) = formula(effects_program.supervision / effects_program.parallel_now
        + effects_program.compute_now / leadership.expert_cost)  @stage_ai
        "The same share today"
    readonly unit_cost: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.ai_share + this.ai_share * this.overhead)  @stage_ai
        "Cost of the work for the attack as a share of its cost by hand: the human part and the AI part"
    readonly unit_cost_now: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.ai_now + this.ai_now
        * this.overhead_now)  @stage_ai
        "The same share today"
    readonly target_progress: formula(fraction) = formula((ai_tools.payload_progress
        if this.target_payload_path else ai_tools.progress) if this.split_ai else this.progress)  @stage_split
        "AI progress that reaches the work for each target"
    readonly target_share: formula(fraction) = formula(this.target_ai_now + (this.target_ai_end
        - this.target_ai_now) * this.target_progress if this.split_ai else this.ai_share)  @stage_split
        "Share of the work for each target that AI does"
    readonly target_share_now: formula(fraction) = formula(this.target_ai_now if this.split_ai
        else this.ai_now)  @stage_split
        "The same share today"
    readonly target_cost: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.target_share + this.target_share
        * this.overhead)  @stage_split
        "Cost of the work for each target as a share of its cost by hand"
    readonly target_cost_now: formula(ratio) = formula(1 - this.target_share_now + this.target_share_now
        * this.overhead_now)  @stage_split
        "The same share today"
    readonly cost: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((this.work * this.unit_cost + this.target_work
        * this.stage_targets * this.target_cost) * (effects_program.waiting if this.held else 1))  @stage_cost
        "Expert work of the stage for one attack"
    readonly cost_now: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((this.work * this.unit_cost_now
        + this.target_work * effects_program.targets_now * this.target_cost_now)
        * (effects_program.waiting_now if this.held else 1))  @stage_cost
        "The same work today"
    input shared_work: bool = false  @access_lessons
        "The work is the same as surveillance's: its lessons come from attacks and from surveillance"
    readonly learning: formula(ratio) = formula(effects_program.access_factor if this.shared_work else 1
        - effects_program.cost_learning * effects_program.gain)  @cost_learning
        "Share of the stage's work that is left after lessons"
    readonly learned_cost: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(this.cost
        * this.learning)  @cost_learning
        "Expert work of the stage for one attack, after lessons"
    input analyst: bool = false  @expert_pools
        "Analysts do the work, not operators"
    readonly operator_cost: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((0 person * years/operation)
        if this.analyst else this.learned_cost)  @expert_pools
        "Operators' work of the stage for one attack, after lessons"
    readonly operator_cost_now: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((0 person * years/operation)
        if this.analyst else this.cost_now)  @expert_pools
        "The same work today"
    readonly analyst_cost_now: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(this.cost_now if this.analyst
        else (0 person * years/operation))  @expert_pools
        "Analysts' work of the stage for one attack today"
    readonly effects_cost: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((0 person * years/operation)
        if this.shared_work or this.analyst else this.cost)  @cost_learning
        "The operators' work of the stage before lessons, where the lessons of attacks cut it"
    readonly effects_cost_now: formula(person * years/operation) = formula((0 person * years/operation)
        if this.shared_work or this.analyst else this.cost_now)  @cost_learning
        "The same work today"
    readonly ai_work: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(this.work * this.ai_share + this.target_work
        * this.stage_targets * this.target_share)  @stage_ai
        "Work of one attack that AI does, as the expert work by hand that it replaces"
    readonly time: formula(years) = formula(this.time_now * exp(this.progress * ln(this.time_end
        / this.time_now)))  @lead_time
        "Time that the work takes"
    readonly lead_term: formula(years) = formula(this.time if this.builds else 0 years)  @lead_time
        "The work's part of the time to build an attack"
    readonly lead_term_now: formula(years) = formula(this.time_now if this.builds else 0 years)  @lead_time
        "The same part today"

planning_stage: Stage
    "Target analysis, legal review and approval."
    analyst = true  @expert_pools
    work = 1 person * years/operation  @planning_stage
    target_work = 0.5 person * years/target  @planning_stage
    ai_end = 0.2  @planning_stage
    payload_path = true  @planning_stage
    split_ai = true  @planning_ai
    target_ai_now = 0.2  @planning_ai
    target_ai_end = 0.75  @planning_ai

access_stage: Stage
    "Gaining and keeping access to the targets."
    work = 0.3 person * years/operation  @access_stage
    target_work = 1.2 person * years/target  @access_stage
    ai_now = 0.25  @access_stage
    ai_end = 0.87  @access_stage
    held = true  @access_stage
    builds = true  @access_stage
    time_now = 0.55 years  @access_stage
    time_end = 0.01 years  @access_stage
    shared_work = true  @access_lessons

payload_stage: Stage
    "Building and testing the effect."
    work = 1.6 person * years/operation  @payload_stage
    target_work = 0.4 person * years/target  @payload_stage
    ai_now = 0.05  @payload_stage
    ai_end = 0.57  @payload_stage
    payload_path = true  @payload_stage
    held = true  @payload_stage
    builds = true  @payload_stage
    time_now = 0.2 years  @payload_stage
    time_end = 0.07 years  @payload_stage

execution_stage: Stage
    "Running the attack at its time."
    work = 0.4 person * years/operation  @execution_stage
    target_work = 0.1 person * years/target  @execution_stage
    ai_now = 0.3  @execution_stage
    ai_end = 0.9  @execution_stage

assessment_stage: Stage
    "Damage assessment."
    analyst = true  @expert_pools
    work = 1 person * years/operation  @assessment_stage
    target_work = 0.7 person * years/target  @assessment_stage
    ai_end = 0.3  @assessment_stage
    payload_path = true  @assessment_stage
    split_ai = true  @assessment_ai
    target_ai_now = 0.1  @assessment_ai
    target_ai_end = 0.6  @assessment_ai
    target_payload_path = true  @assessment_ai
    time_now = 0.33 years  @assessment_time
    time_end = 0.16 years  @assessment_time
    stage_targets = formula(effects_program.assessed_size)  @assessment_time

Pool:  @capability_pool
    "The capabilities of one step of an operation. A capability is a flaw that the defenders do not know, with
        the tools that use it, and it burns as a whole. It is never used, used by surveillance, used in an
        attack, or burned. Used in an attack, it is held by an attack underway, or kept from an earlier attack
        that was not exposed."
    role researchers
    input known: fraction = 0.8 in [0, 0.99]  @one_day_chance
        "Share of the needs of the step that a known flaw or the target's own functions can serve"
    input patch_pace: ratio = 1 in [0, 2]  @one_day_chance
        "Pace at which targets fix known flaws at this step, as a multiple of the defenders' fix rate"
    readonly step_time: formula(years) = formula(access_stage.time)  @one_day_chance
        "Time from the start of the step until the force uses the flaw"
    readonly step_time_now: formula(years) = formula(access_stage.time_now)  @one_day_chance
        "The same time today"
    readonly open: formula(fraction) = formula(defenders.residual + (1 - defenders.residual)
        * exp(-defenders.fix_rate * this.patch_pace * this.step_time))  @one_day_chance
        "Share of targets that have not fixed a known flaw by the time of its use"
    readonly open_now: formula(fraction) = formula(defenders.residual + (1 - defenders.residual)
        * exp(-defenders.fix_rate * this.patch_pace * this.step_time_now))  @one_day_chance
        "The same share today"
    readonly one_day: formula(fraction) = formula(this.known * this.open)  @one_day_chance
        "Chance that a known flaw serves a need of the step: a one-day, which takes nothing from the pool"
    readonly one_day_now: formula(fraction) = formula(this.known * this.open_now)  @one_day_chance
        "The same chance today"
    # What the missions need from the pool: the zero-days of the units that pass the step. Each instance says.
    readonly attack_need: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(0 capabilities/year)  @capability_use
        "Zero-days that attacks need in a year at the step, for attacks that wait before they are made"
    readonly attack_need_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(0 capabilities/year)  @capability_use
        "Zero-days that attacks that wait need in a year at the step today"
    readonly at_once_need: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(0 capabilities/year)  @capability_use
        "Zero-days that attacks need in a year at the step, for attacks made as soon as they are ready"
    readonly at_once_need_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(0 capabilities/year)  @capability_use
        "Zero-days that attacks made at once need in a year at the step today"
    readonly spy_need: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(0 capabilities/year)  @capability_use
        "Zero-days that surveillance needs in a year at the step"
    readonly spy_need_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(0 capabilities/year)  @capability_use
        "Zero-days that surveillance needs in a year at the step today"
    readonly holders: formula(operations) = formula(0 operations)  @capability_burn
        "Attacks underway that hold capabilities of the pool"
    readonly holders_now: formula(operations) = formula(0 operations)  @capability_burn
        "Attacks underway today that hold capabilities of the pool"
    readonly made: formula(operations/year) = formula(0 operations/year)  @capability_burn
        "Attacks made in a year that hold capabilities of the pool"
    readonly made_now: formula(operations/year) = formula(0 operations/year)  @capability_burn
        "Attacks made in a year today that hold capabilities of the pool"
    readonly made_rate: formula(per_year) = formula(this.made / max(this.holders,
        0.001 operations))  @capability_burn
        "Share of the attacks that hold capabilities of the pool that the force makes in a year"
    readonly made_rate_now: formula(per_year) = formula(this.made_now / max(this.holders_now,
        0.001 operations))  @capability_burn
        "The same share today"
    # Today's shares of the sources of a zero-day. A source that the step does not have is zero.
    readonly attack_spy_now: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.spy_source)  @capability_sources
        "Share of an attack's zero-days at the step today that surveillance already uses"
    readonly attack_kept_now: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.reuse_source)  @capability_sources
        "Share of an attack's zero-days at the step today that an earlier attack used and did not burn"
    readonly spy_own_now: formula(fraction) = formula(surveillance_program.own_source)  @capability_sources
        "Share of surveillance's zero-days at the step today that it already uses"
    readonly spy_kept_now: formula(fraction) = formula(surveillance_program.attack_source)  @capability_sources
        "Share of surveillance's zero-days at the step today that an earlier attack used and did not burn"
    # Today is a rest point of the pool: each stock's inflows equal its outflows at today's needs and shares.
    readonly held_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.attack_need_now / (this.made_rate_now
        + defenders.use_rediscovery_now))  @capability_rest
        "Capabilities held by attacks underway today"
    # The kept capabilities that surveillance also uses are in use, so they are lost at the in-use rate, and
    # the others at the stockpile rate. Their balances give the shared share as the positive root of
    # B·Δ·φ² + b·φ − Q·δ_s = 0, with b = δ_u·R + B·δ_s − Q·Δ and Δ = δ_u − δ_s.
    readonly kept_net_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula((1 - effects_program.exposure)
        * (this.made_rate_now * this.held_now + this.at_once_need_now * (1 - this.attack_spy_now
        - this.attack_kept_now)) - (this.attack_need_now + effects_program.exposure * this.at_once_need_now)
        * this.attack_kept_now)  @capability_rest
        "Capabilities that the kept stock gains today, less the attacks' draws from it"
    readonly kept_shared_in_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula((1 - effects_program.exposure)
        * this.made_rate_now * this.attack_need_now * this.attack_spy_now / (this.made_rate_now
        + defenders.use_rediscovery_now) + this.spy_need_now * this.spy_kept_now)  @capability_rest
        "Capabilities that enter the kept stock that surveillance also uses, today"
    readonly kept_shared_draw_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(this.attack_need_now
        * this.attack_kept_now * (1 - (1 - effects_program.exposure) * this.made_rate_now
        / (this.made_rate_now + defenders.use_rediscovery_now)))  @capability_rest
        "Net draw of attacks on the kept stock that surveillance also uses, for each unit of its share"
    readonly use_gap_now: formula(per_year) = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery_now
        - defenders.rediscovery_now)  @capability_rest
        "How much faster a flaw in use is lost than a stockpiled flaw, today"
    readonly kept_root_b: formula(per_year) = formula((defenders.use_rediscovery_now * this.kept_net_now
        + this.kept_shared_draw_now * defenders.rediscovery_now - this.kept_shared_in_now * this.use_gap_now)
        / (1 capabilities/year))  @capability_rest
        "Linear term of the balance of the kept stock that surveillance also uses, per capability a year"
    readonly kept_shared_part_now: formula(fraction) = formula(2 * this.kept_shared_in_now
        / (1 capabilities/year) * defenders.rediscovery_now / max(this.kept_root_b
        + sqrt(this.kept_root_b ** 2 + 4 * this.kept_shared_draw_now / (1 capabilities/year)
        * this.use_gap_now * this.kept_shared_in_now / (1 capabilities/year) * defenders.rediscovery_now),
        1e-30 per_year))  @capability_rest
        "Share of the kept capabilities today that surveillance also uses"
    readonly kept_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.kept_net_now / (defenders.rediscovery_now
        + this.kept_shared_part_now * this.use_gap_now))  @capability_rest
        "Capabilities kept today from earlier attacks that were not exposed"
    readonly kept_shared_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.kept_shared_part_now
        * this.kept_now)  @capability_rest
        "Kept capabilities today that surveillance also uses"
    readonly kept_attack_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.kept_now
        - this.kept_shared_now)  @capability_rest
        "Kept capabilities today that only attacks use"
    readonly held_shared_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.attack_need_now * (this.attack_spy_now
        + this.attack_kept_now * this.kept_shared_part_now) / (this.made_rate_now
        + defenders.use_rediscovery_now))  @capability_rest
        "Capabilities held by attacks underway today that surveillance also uses"
    readonly held_attack_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.held_now
        - this.held_shared_now)  @capability_rest
        "Capabilities held by attacks underway today that only attacks use"
    readonly spy_used_now: formula(capabilities) = formula((this.spy_need_now * (1 - this.spy_own_now
        - this.spy_kept_now) - this.attack_need_now * this.attack_spy_now)
        / defenders.use_rediscovery_now)  @capability_rest
        "Capabilities that surveillance uses today and that no attack has used"
    readonly fresh_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(researchers.reserve_time * ((this.attack_need_now
        + this.at_once_need_now) * (1 - this.attack_spy_now - this.attack_kept_now) + this.spy_need_now * (1
        - this.spy_own_now - this.spy_kept_now)))  @capability_reserve
        "Capabilities never used today"
    assert this.attack_spy_now <= 0 or this.spy_used_now > 0 capabilities  @capability_rest
        "Attacks take more of surveillance's capabilities today than surveillance draws: lower the share of an
            attack's zero-days that surveillance already uses."
    assert this.attack_kept_now <= 0 or this.kept_now > 0 capabilities  @capability_rest
        "Attacks reuse more capabilities today than the attacks that stay hidden keep: lower the share of an
            attack's zero-days that it reuses."
    assert this.spy_kept_now <= 0 or this.kept_attack_now > 0 capabilities  @capability_rest
        "Surveillance takes more of the attacks' kept capabilities today than they keep: lower the share of
            surveillance's zero-days that come from attacks."
    # A need is served by a capability already in use as if each capability in use were one independent try:
    # with chance 1 - exp(-y), where y grows in proportion to the capabilities in use and today's y gives
    # today's shares. The rest of the need takes a never-used capability.
    readonly attack_scale_now: formula(ratio) = formula(-ln(1 - this.attack_spy_now
        - this.attack_kept_now))  @capability_sources
        "Tries of an attack's need on the capabilities already in use today"
    readonly kept: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.kept_shared + this.kept_attack)  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities kept from earlier attacks that were not exposed"
    readonly kept_shared_share: formula(fraction) = formula(this.kept_shared / max(this.kept,
        1e-9 capabilities))  @capability_pool
        "Share of the kept capabilities that surveillance also uses"
    readonly attack_spy_tries: formula(ratio) = formula(this.attack_scale_now * this.attack_spy_now
        / max(this.attack_spy_now + this.attack_kept_now, 1e-12) * this.spy_used / max(this.spy_used_now,
        1e-6 capabilities))  @capability_sources
        "Tries of an attack's need on surveillance's capabilities"
    readonly attack_kept_tries: formula(ratio) = formula(this.attack_scale_now * this.attack_kept_now
        / max(this.attack_spy_now + this.attack_kept_now, 1e-12) * this.kept / max(this.kept_now,
        1e-6 capabilities))  @capability_sources
        "Tries of an attack's need on the kept capabilities"
    readonly attack_tries: formula(ratio) = formula(this.attack_spy_tries
        + this.attack_kept_tries)  @capability_sources
        "Tries of an attack's need on the capabilities already in use"
    readonly attack_from_spy: formula(fraction) = formula(-expm1(-this.attack_tries) * this.attack_spy_tries
        / max(this.attack_tries, 1e-12))  @capability_sources
        "Share of an attack's zero-days that surveillance already uses"
    readonly attack_from_kept: formula(fraction) = formula(-expm1(-this.attack_tries) * this.attack_kept_tries
        / max(this.attack_tries, 1e-12))  @capability_sources
        "Share of an attack's zero-days that an earlier attack used and did not burn"
    readonly attack_from_fresh: formula(fraction) = formula(exp(-this.attack_tries))  @capability_sources
        "Share of an attack's zero-days that are never used"
    readonly spy_scale_now: formula(ratio) = formula(-ln(1 - this.spy_own_now
        - this.spy_kept_now))  @capability_sources
        "Tries of surveillance's need on the capabilities already in use today"
    readonly spy_in_use: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.spy_used + this.held_shared
        + this.kept_shared)  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities that surveillance uses"
    readonly spy_in_use_now: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.spy_used_now + this.held_shared_now
        + this.kept_shared_now)  @capability_rest
        "The same capabilities today"
    readonly spy_own_tries: formula(ratio) = formula(this.spy_scale_now * this.spy_own_now
        / max(this.spy_own_now + this.spy_kept_now, 1e-12) * this.spy_in_use / max(this.spy_in_use_now,
        1e-6 capabilities))  @capability_sources
        "Tries of surveillance's need on its own capabilities"
    readonly spy_kept_tries: formula(ratio) = formula(this.spy_scale_now * this.spy_kept_now
        / max(this.spy_own_now + this.spy_kept_now, 1e-12) * this.kept_attack / max(this.kept_attack_now,
        1e-6 capabilities))  @capability_sources
        "Tries of surveillance's need on the capabilities that only attacks used"
    readonly spy_tries: formula(ratio) = formula(this.spy_own_tries
        + this.spy_kept_tries)  @capability_sources
        "Tries of surveillance's need on the capabilities already in use"
    readonly spy_from_kept: formula(fraction) = formula(-expm1(-this.spy_tries) * this.spy_kept_tries
        / max(this.spy_tries, 1e-12))  @capability_sources
        "Share of surveillance's zero-days that an earlier attack used and did not burn"
    readonly spy_from_fresh: formula(fraction) = formula(exp(-this.spy_tries))  @capability_sources
        "Share of surveillance's zero-days that are never used"
    # The parts of an attack step's units by the source of their zero-days. Each part moves with its source.
    readonly attack_part_spy: formula(fraction) = formula((1 - this.one_day)
        * this.attack_from_spy)  @capability_sources
        "Share of the units of an attack step whose zero-days surveillance already uses"
    readonly attack_part_kept_shared: formula(fraction) = formula((1 - this.one_day) * this.attack_from_kept
        * this.kept_shared_share)  @capability_sources
        "Share of the units of an attack step that reuse kept capabilities that surveillance also uses"
    readonly attack_part_kept_attack: formula(fraction) = formula((1 - this.one_day) * this.attack_from_kept
        * (1 - this.kept_shared_share))  @capability_sources
        "Share of the units of an attack step that reuse kept capabilities that only attacks used"
    readonly fresh_draws: formula(capabilities/year) = formula((this.attack_need + this.at_once_need)
        * this.attack_from_fresh + this.spy_need * this.spy_from_fresh)  @capability_pool
        "Never-used capabilities that the missions ask from the pool in a year"
    readonly available: formula(fraction) = formula(min(1, this.fresh / max(this.fresh_draws
        * researchers.supply_time, 1e-9 capabilities)))  @capability_pool
        "Share of the asks for never-used capabilities that the pool serves now"
    readonly attack_served: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - (1 - this.one_day) * this.attack_from_fresh * (1
        - this.available))  @capability_pool
        "Share of the units of an attack step that the pool lets pass now"
    readonly spy_served: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - (1 - this.one_day) * this.spy_from_fresh * (1
        - this.available))  @capability_pool
        "Share of the units of a surveillance step that the pool lets pass now"
    readonly attack_part_new: formula(fraction) = formula((1 - this.one_day) * this.attack_from_fresh
        * this.available)  @capability_sources
        "Share of the units of an attack step whose zero-days no one has used"
    # The parts of a surveillance step's units by the source of their zero-days. Each part moves with its source.
    readonly spy_part_free: formula(fraction) = formula(this.one_day + (1 - this.one_day) * (1
        - this.spy_from_kept - this.spy_from_fresh))  @capability_sources
        "Share of the units of a surveillance step that take nothing from the pool: one-days, and capabilities
            that surveillance already uses"
    readonly spy_part_kept: formula(fraction) = formula((1 - this.one_day)
        * this.spy_from_kept)  @capability_sources
        "Share of the units of a surveillance step that take kept capabilities of earlier attacks"
    readonly spy_part_new: formula(fraction) = formula((1 - this.one_day) * this.spy_from_fresh
        * this.available)  @capability_sources
        "Share of the units of a surveillance step whose zero-days no one has used"
    readonly in_attacks: formula(capabilities) = formula(this.held_shared + this.held_attack
        + this.kept)  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities used in an attack and not burned"
    # Exposed attacks burn the capabilities that they hold. Where surveillance also uses one, the defenders find
    # a share of the accesses that run on it.
    readonly burn_loss: formula(per_year) = formula(surveillance_program.find_share * effects_program.exposure
        * this.made_rate * this.held_shared * (1 - this.one_day) / max(this.spy_in_use,
        0.001 capabilities))  @capability_burn
        "Share of surveillance's accesses that the defenders find in a year through the capabilities that
            exposed attacks burn and surveillance also uses"
    readonly burn_loss_now: formula(per_year) = formula(surveillance_program.find_share
        * effects_program.exposure * this.made_rate_now * this.held_shared_now * (1 - this.one_day_now)
        / max(this.spy_in_use_now, 0.001 capabilities))  @capability_burn
        "The same share today"
    readonly research_need: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(max(this.fresh_draws + defenders.rediscovery
        * this.fresh + (researchers.reserve_time * this.fresh_draws - this.fresh) / researchers.reserve_time,
        0 capabilities/year))  @research_split
        "Capabilities that the pool asks from the researchers in a year: those that the missions take from it,
            and those that others find"
    readonly research_need_now: formula(capabilities/year) = formula((this.attack_need_now
        + this.at_once_need_now) * (1 - this.attack_spy_now - this.attack_kept_now) + this.spy_need_now * (1
        - this.spy_own_now - this.spy_kept_now) + defenders.rediscovery_now * this.fresh_now)  @research_split
        "The same capabilities today"
    fresh: capabilities = this.fresh_now in [0 capabilities,
        10000000 capabilities] scale 100 capabilities  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities never used"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.fresh_draws * this.available + defenders.rediscovery
            * this.fresh)  @capability_pool
    spy_used: capabilities = this.spy_used_now in [0 capabilities,
        10000000 capabilities] scale 100 capabilities  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities that surveillance uses and that no attack has used"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.attack_need * this.attack_from_spy + defenders.use_rediscovery
            * this.spy_used)  @capability_pool
    held_shared: capabilities = this.held_shared_now in [0 capabilities,
        10000000 capabilities] scale 100 capabilities  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities held by attacks underway that surveillance also uses"
        outflow.capacity = formula((this.made_rate + defenders.use_rediscovery)
            * this.held_shared)  @capability_pool
    held_attack: capabilities = this.held_attack_now in [0 capabilities,
        10000000 capabilities] scale 100 capabilities  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities held by attacks underway that only attacks use"
        outflow.capacity = formula((this.made_rate + defenders.use_rediscovery)
            * this.held_attack)  @capability_pool
    kept_shared: capabilities = this.kept_shared_now in [0 capabilities,
        10000000 capabilities] scale 100 capabilities  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities kept from earlier attacks that were not exposed, which surveillance also uses"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.attack_need * this.attack_from_kept * this.kept_shared_share
            + defenders.use_rediscovery * this.kept_shared)  @capability_pool
    kept_attack: capabilities = this.kept_attack_now in [0 capabilities,
        10000000 capabilities] scale 100 capabilities  @capability_pool
        "Capabilities kept from earlier attacks that were not exposed, which only attacks use"
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.attack_need * this.attack_from_kept * (1 - this.kept_shared_share)
            + this.at_once_need * this.attack_from_kept * effects_program.exposure + this.spy_need
            * this.spy_from_kept + defenders.rediscovery * this.kept_attack)  @capability_pool
    burned: capabilities = 0 capabilities scale 10000 capabilities  @capability_burn
        "Capabilities that exposed attacks burned since the start"
    flow research: SOURCE -> this.fresh  @research_split
        "The researchers find new capabilities for the pool."
        request = formula(this.research_need * min(1, researchers.output / max(researchers.need,
            1e-9 capabilities/year)))
        capacity = formula(this.research_need * min(1, researchers.output / max(researchers.need,
            1e-9 capabilities/year)))
    flow burn_shared: this.held_shared -> this.burned  @capability_burn
        "Exposed attacks burn the capabilities that they hold and that surveillance also uses."
        request = formula(effects_program.exposure * this.made_rate * this.held_shared)
        capacity = formula(effects_program.exposure * this.made_rate * this.held_shared)
    flow keep_shared: this.held_shared -> this.kept_shared  @capability_burn
        "Attacks that stay hidden keep them."
        request = formula((1 - effects_program.exposure) * this.made_rate * this.held_shared)
        capacity = formula((1 - effects_program.exposure) * this.made_rate * this.held_shared)
    flow burn_attack: this.held_attack -> this.burned  @capability_burn
        "Exposed attacks burn the capabilities that they hold and that only attacks use."
        request = formula(effects_program.exposure * this.made_rate * this.held_attack)
        capacity = formula(effects_program.exposure * this.made_rate * this.held_attack)
    flow keep_attack: this.held_attack -> this.kept_attack  @capability_burn
        "Attacks that stay hidden keep them."
        request = formula((1 - effects_program.exposure) * this.made_rate * this.held_attack)
        capacity = formula((1 - effects_program.exposure) * this.made_rate * this.held_attack)
    flow found_fresh: this.fresh -> SINK  @rediscovery
        "Others find and disclose flaws that no one has used."
        request = formula(defenders.rediscovery * this.fresh)
        capacity = formula(defenders.rediscovery * this.fresh)
    flow found_spy: this.spy_used -> SINK  @rediscovery
        "Others find and disclose flaws that surveillance uses."
        request = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.spy_used)
        capacity = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.spy_used)
    flow found_held_shared: this.held_shared -> SINK  @rediscovery
        "Others find and disclose flaws that attacks underway hold."
        request = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.held_shared)
        capacity = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.held_shared)
    flow found_held_attack: this.held_attack -> SINK  @rediscovery
        "Others find and disclose flaws that attacks underway hold."
        request = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.held_attack)
        capacity = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.held_attack)
    flow found_kept_shared: this.kept_shared -> SINK  @rediscovery
        "Others find and disclose flaws that attacks kept."
        request = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.kept_shared)
        capacity = formula(defenders.use_rediscovery * this.kept_shared)
    flow found_kept_attack: this.kept_attack -> SINK  @rediscovery
        "Others find and disclose flaws that attacks kept."
        request = formula(defenders.rediscovery * this.kept_attack)
        capacity = formula(defenders.rediscovery * this.kept_attack)
    # Each limit is all that the flows ask, so it caps none of them; at an empty stock they share what is left.

access_pool: Pool
    "Capabilities that get access to a target network. Surveillance and attacks share them."
    step_time = formula(effects_program.initial_time)  @one_day_chance
    step_time_now = formula(effects_program.initial_time_now)  @one_day_chance
    attack_need = formula(effects_program.access_rate * effects_program.access_target_need * (1
        - this.one_day))  @capability_use
    attack_need_now = formula(effects_program.attacks_now * effects_program.types_now * (1
        - this.one_day_now))  @capability_use
    spy_need = formula(surveillance_program.access_rate * (1 capabilities/access) * (1
        - this.one_day))  @capability_use
    spy_need_now = formula(surveillance_program.builds_now * (1 capabilities/access) * (1
        - this.one_day_now))  @capability_use
    holders = formula(effects_program.access_attacks + effects_program.positioned_attacks
        + effects_program.held_ready)  @capability_burn
    holders_now = formula(effects_program.attacks_now * (effects_program.movement_time_now
        + payload_stage.time_now + effects_program.built_ahead_now
        / effects_program.use_rate))  @capability_burn
    made = formula(effects_program.attacks)  @capability_burn
    made_now = formula(effects_program.attacks_now)  @capability_burn

movement_pool: Pool
    "Capabilities that move inside a network from the first access to the systems that the operation needs.
        Surveillance and attacks share them."
    known = 0.9  @one_day_chance
    patch_pace = 0.5  @one_day_chance
    step_time = formula(effects_program.movement_time)  @one_day_chance
    step_time_now = formula(effects_program.movement_time_now)  @one_day_chance
    attack_need = formula(effects_program.movement_rate * effects_program.movement_target_need * (1
        - this.one_day))  @capability_use
    attack_need_now = formula(effects_program.attacks_now * effects_program.types_now * (1
        - this.one_day_now))  @capability_use
    spy_need = formula(surveillance_program.deploy_rate * (1 capabilities/access) * (1
        - this.one_day))  @capability_use
    spy_need_now = formula(surveillance_program.deployed_now * (1 capabilities/access) * (1
        - this.one_day_now))  @capability_use
    holders = formula(effects_program.positioned_attacks + effects_program.held_ready)  @capability_burn
    holders_now = formula(effects_program.attacks_now * (payload_stage.time_now
        + effects_program.built_ahead_now / effects_program.use_rate))  @capability_burn
    made = formula(effects_program.attacks)  @capability_burn
    made_now = formula(effects_program.attacks_now)  @capability_burn

effect_pool: Pool
    "Capabilities that give the effect of an attack on the systems of its targets. Only attacks use them."
    patch_pace = 0.2  @one_day_chance
    step_time = formula(payload_stage.time)  @one_day_chance
    step_time_now = formula(payload_stage.time_now)  @one_day_chance
    attack_need = formula(effects_program.hold_rate * effects_program.positioned_types * (1
        - this.one_day))  @capability_use
    attack_need_now = formula(effects_program.built_ahead_now * effects_program.attacks_now
        * effects_program.types_now * (1 - this.one_day_now))  @capability_use
    at_once_need = formula(effects_program.now_rate * effects_program.positioned_types * (1
        - this.one_day))  @capability_use
    at_once_need_now = formula((1 - effects_program.built_ahead_now) * effects_program.attacks_now
        * effects_program.types_now * (1 - this.one_day_now))  @capability_use
    holders = formula(effects_program.held_ready)  @capability_burn
    holders_now = formula(effects_program.built_ahead_now * effects_program.attacks_now
        / effects_program.use_rate)  @capability_burn
    made = formula(effects_program.moment_rate * effects_program.held_ready
        * effects_program.execution_served)  @capability_burn
    made_now = formula(effects_program.built_ahead_now * effects_program.attacks_now)  @capability_burn
    attack_spy_now = formula(0)  @capability_sources
    spy_own_now = formula(0)  @capability_sources
    spy_kept_now = formula(0)  @capability_sources

collection_pool: Pool
    "Capabilities that collect what surveillance needs from a network and send it out. Only surveillance uses
        them."
    known = 0.9  @one_day_chance
    patch_pace = 0  @one_day_chance
    spy_need = formula(surveillance_program.deploy_rate * (1 capabilities/access) * (1
        - this.one_day))  @capability_use
    spy_need_now = formula(surveillance_program.deployed_now * (1 capabilities/access) * (1
        - this.one_day_now))  @capability_use
    attack_spy_now = formula(0)  @capability_sources
    attack_kept_now = formula(0)  @capability_sources
    spy_kept_now = formula(0)  @capability_sources

Channel:  @attribution_channels
    "A kind of evidence by which other countries attribute an attack."
    role other_states
    input chance_now: fraction = 0.2 in [0, 0.9]  @attribution_channels
        "Chance today that this evidence attributes an attack"
    input chance_end: fraction = 0.2 in [0, 0.9]  @attribution_channels
        "The same chance at the end of AI progress"
    readonly chance: formula(fraction) = formula(this.chance_now + (this.chance_end - this.chance_now)
        * ai_tools.progress)  @attribution_channels
        "Chance that this evidence attributes an attack"
    readonly miss: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(1 - this.chance))  @attribution_channels
        "Log-chance that this evidence does not attribute an attack"
    readonly miss_now: formula(ratio) = formula(ln(1 - this.chance_now))  @attribution_channels
        "The same log-chance today"

tools_channel: Channel
    "The code and tools of an attack."
    chance_now = 0.4  @tools_channel
    chance_end = 0.05  @tools_channel

infrastructure_channel: Channel
    "The servers and accounts that an attack uses."
    chance_now = 0.3  @infrastructure_channel
    chance_end = 0.3  @infrastructure_channel

operators_channel: Channel
    "The habits of the operators: their hours, their language, their mistakes."

targeting_channel: Channel
    "The choice of targets and of the time, which points to whom the attack serves."

attacks_per_year: formula(operations/year) = formula(effects_program.attacks) in [0,]  @attack_pipeline
    "Attacks that the force makes in a year"
attacks_started: formula(operations/year) = formula(effects_program.starts) in [0,]  @attack_count
    "Attacks that the force starts to build in a year"
capabilities_held: formula(operations) = formula(effects_program.held_ready) in [0,]  @held_capabilities
    "Attacks held ready for their moment"
targets_in_build: formula(targets) = formula(effects_program.in_access + effects_program.accesses
    + effects_program.positioned) in [0,]  @attack_pipeline
    "Targets that the force works on before their attacks are ready: gaining access, moving inside the network
        or building the effect"
attacks_in_assessment: formula(operations) = formula(effects_program.assessing) in [0,]  @assessment_time
    "Attacks whose damage the force is assessing"
share_on_attacks: formula(fraction) = formula(leadership.attack_share) in [0,]  @split_balance
    "Share of the operators on attacks"
expert_ratio: formula(ratio) = formula(surveillance_program.spying_experts
    / leadership.attack_experts) in [0,]  @split_balance
    "Operators on surveillance for each operator on attacks"
value_to_cost: formula(ratio) = formula(effects_program.attack_value / (effects_program.attack_cost
    + leadership.attack_experts * surveillance_program.spying_return)) in [0,]  @value_basis
    "Value of the attacks against their full cost: sanctions, burned access and the surveillance that the
        operators on attacks do not do"
lesson_weight: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.weight) in [0,]  @learning_curve
    "Weight of lessons in the force's choices"
plan_chance: formula(fraction) = formula(military_planners.best_chance) in [0,]  @plan_test
    "Chance that the best plan of cyber attacks meets its plan"
best_plan_length: formula(days) = formula(military_planners.best_length) in [0,]  @plan_test
    "Length of the best plan of cyber attacks"
passes: formula(ratio) = formula(military_planners.passes_in_a_row) in [0,]  @doctrine_time
    "Planning reviews in a row that a plan passes"
misses: formula(ratio) = formula(military_planners.misses_in_a_row) in [0,]  @doctrine_lapse
    "Planning reviews in a row that every plan misses"
doctrine_length: formula(days) = formula(military_planners.formed_length) in [0,]  @plan_test
    "Length of the plan that doctrine last formed around"
doctrine_counts: formula(fraction) = formula(1 if military_planners.doctrine == FORMED
    else 0) in [0,]  @doctrine_time
    "Whether military plans count on cyber attacks: 1 when doctrine has formed and holds, else 0"
plan_margin: formula(ratio) = formula(military_planners.best_chance
    - military_planners.acceptance)  @plan_test
    "Chance that the best plan of cyber attacks meets its plan, less the chance that the planners need"
attacks_rise: formula(fraction) = formula(1 if leadership.attack_share > operators.share_now
    else 0) in [0,]  @split_balance
    "Whether the leaders put more of the operators on attacks than today: 1 if they do, else 0"
new_access: formula(fraction) = formula(1 - effects_program.built_ahead) in [0,]  @waiting_cost
    "Share of attacks from access built for them on demand"
lessons_gained: formula(targets/year) = formula(effects_program.learn_rate) in [0,]  @learning_basis
    "Lessons gained in a year"
lessons_lost: formula(targets/year) = formula(effects_program.loss_rate) in [0,]  @forgetting
    "Lessons lost in a year"
assessment_signal: formula(ratio) = formula(1 / effects_program.assessment_spread) in [0,]  @assessment_noise
    "Signal-to-noise ratio of the yearly damage assessment"
spending: formula(USD2025_bn/yr) = formula((leadership.attack_experts + effects_program.analysis_done)
    * leadership.expert_cost) in [0,]  @expert_cost
    "Spending on the operators and analysts of attacks in a year"
targets_hit: formula(targets/year) = formula(effects_program.hits) in [0,]  @value_basis
    "Targets hit in a year"
targets_per_attack: formula(targets/operation) = formula(effects_program.attack_targets) in [0,]  @targets_basis
    "Targets of one attack"
cost_per_attack: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(effects_program.cost) in [0,]  @stage_cost
    "Expert work for one attack"
cost_per_target: formula(person * years/target) = formula(effects_program.cost
    / effects_program.attack_targets) in [0,]  @stage_cost
    "Expert work for each target of an attack"
build_time: formula(years) = formula(effects_program.lead_time) in [0,]  @lead_time
    "Time to build the access and the effect of one attack"
ai_share_of_work: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.automation) in [0,]  @stage_ai
    "Share of the work of an attack that AI does"
compute_spending: formula(USD2025_bn/yr) = formula(effects_program.compute_spending) in [0,]  @stage_compute
    "Spending on the compute of AI work in a year"
within_attack_correlation: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.within_correlation) in [0,]  @outcome_correlation
    "Correlation of the outcomes on the targets of one attack"
attribution_chance: formula(fraction) = formula(other_states.attribution) in [0,]  @attribution_channels
    "Chance that other countries attribute an attack"
planning_work: formula(person
    * years/operation) = formula(planning_stage.learned_cost) in [0,]  @planning_stage
    "Expert work of target analysis and approval for one attack"
access_work: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(access_stage.learned_cost) in [0,]  @access_stage
    "Expert work of access for one attack"
payload_work: formula(person * years/operation) = formula(payload_stage.learned_cost) in [0,]  @payload_stage
    "Expert work of building and testing the effect for one attack"
execution_work: formula(person
    * years/operation) = formula(execution_stage.learned_cost) in [0,]  @execution_stage
    "Expert work of running one attack"
assessment_work: formula(person
    * years/operation) = formula(assessment_stage.learned_cost) in [0,]  @assessment_stage
    "Expert work of the damage assessment of one attack"
access_time: formula(years) = formula(access_stage.time) in [0,]  @access_stage
    "Time to get access to the targets of an attack"
payload_time: formula(years) = formula(payload_stage.time) in [0,]  @payload_stage
    "Time to build and test the effect of an attack"
assessment_duration: formula(years) = formula(assessment_stage.time) in [0,]  @assessment_time
    "Time of the damage assessment of an attack"
access_lessons: formula(accesses) = formula(effects_program.access_know_how) in [0,]  @access_lessons
    "Lessons of access that the force keeps: accesses built"
success_per_target: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.success) in [0,]  @success_basis
    "Chance that an attack gives its intended effect on one target"
defender_attention: formula(ratio) = formula(defenders.alertness) in [0,]  @alertness_balance
    "Attention of the defenders, as a loss of log-odds of an attack's success"
defender_hardening: formula(ratio) = formula(defenders.hardening) in [0,]  @hardening
    "Lasting capability of the defenders, as a loss of log-odds of an attack's success"
shared_loss: formula(fraction) = formula(day_plan.depth) in [0,]  @shared_depth
    "Share of a plan's effect that a failed shared capability takes"
target_kinds: formula(capabilities/operation) = formula(effects_program.types) in [0,]  @target_kinds
    "Kinds of target system in one attack"
surveillance_accesses: formula(accesses) = formula(surveillance_program.accesses_held
    + surveillance_program.implants) in [0,]  @surveillance_loop
    "Accesses that surveillance holds: those gained and the implants deployed"
accesses_used_share: formula(fraction) = formula(surveillance_program.used
    / max(surveillance_program.implants, 1 accesses)) in [0,]  @surveillance_use
    "Share of its implants that the collection specialists run"
accesses_burned: formula(accesses/year) = formula(surveillance_program.burned_accesses) in [0,]  @capability_burn
    "Accesses of surveillance that attacks burn in a year"
surveillance_implants: formula(accesses) = formula(surveillance_program.implants) in [0,]  @surveillance_loop
    "Implants that surveillance has deployed and collects from"
collected_take: formula(access * years) = formula(surveillance_program.collected) in [0,]  @collection_queue
    "Take that waits for the collection specialists, in access-years"
surveillance_return: formula(sev/person/year) = formula(surveillance_program.spying_return) in [0,]  @surveillance_returns
    "Return of one operator on surveillance"
analysis_served: formula(fraction) = formula(effects_program.starts / max(effects_program.wanted_starts,
    0.001 operations/year)) in [0,]  @analyst_split
    "Share of the attacks that the operators can start that the analysts plan"
idle_operators: formula(people) = formula(operators.idle) in [0,]  @workforce
    "Operators whose hours wait for the analysts to plan their operations"
analysts_on_attacks: formula(fraction) = formula(analysts.attack_share) in [0,]  @analyst_split
    "Share of the analysts on attacks"
surveillance_planned: formula(fraction) = formula(surveillance_program.new_accesses
    / max(surveillance_program.builds, 0.001 accesses/year)) in [0,]  @analyst_split
    "Share of the accesses that surveillance's operators can start that the analysts plan"
research_output: formula(capabilities/year) = formula(researchers.output) in [0,]  @research_yield
    "Capabilities that the researchers find in a year"
capabilities_unused: formula(capabilities) = formula(sum(Pool.instances.fresh)) in [0,]  @capability_pool
    "Unused capabilities"
capabilities_spying: formula(capabilities) = formula(sum(Pool.instances.spy_used)) in [0,]  @capability_pool
    "Capabilities that surveillance runs and that no attack has used"
capabilities_attacks: formula(capabilities) = formula(sum(Pool.instances.in_attacks)) in [0,]  @capability_pool
    "Capabilities used in an attack and not burned: held by attacks underway, or kept from earlier attacks"
capabilities_burned: formula(capabilities) = formula(sum(Pool.instances.burned)) in [0,]  @capability_burn
    "Capabilities that exposed attacks burned since the start"
total_attacks: formula(operations) = formula(effects_program.attacks_made) in [0,]  @attack_count
    "Attacks made since the start"

options "Response":
    "Slow patching":
        "Defenders patch the flaws that attacks use slowly, and their attention fades within about half a
            year."
    "Fast patching":
        "Defenders patch fast, so access that the force builds in advance lasts less long, and their attention
            lasts about a year."
        effects_program.access_decay = 0.6 per_year  @patch_tiers
        defenders.calm_rate = 1 per_year  @patch_tiers
        defenders.alert_now = 0.1  @patch_tiers
        defenders.fix_rate = 15 per_year  @patch_tiers
        surveillance_program.loss_rate = 1 per_year  @patch_tiers

options "AI progress":
    "No AI progress":
        "The cyber force works as today: human experts do the tactical work."
        ai_tools.pace = 0  @no_ai_path
        effects_program.actor = "The human team"
    "Slow AI progress":
        "AI reaches about two thirds of its end in 12 years."
        ai_tools.progress_time = 12 years  @ai_pace
    "Fast AI progress":
        "AI reaches about two thirds of its end in 4 years."
        ai_tools.progress_time = 4 years  @ai_pace
    "AI progress, then costs rise":
        "AI reaches about two thirds of its end in 4 years. From 2038, the costs of attacks rise again and
            take back most of the progress."
        ai_tools.progress_time = 4 years  @ai_pace
        ai_tools.reversal_depth = 0.8  @ai_reversal

options "Analysts' AI":
    "Split AI help":
        "AI does more of the analysts' work for each target than of their work for the whole attack, where
            policy sets the review and the approval."
    "One AI share":
        "AI does one share of each kind of the analysts' work: 20% of the planning and 30% of the damage
            assessment at the end of AI progress, on the slower path."
        planning_stage.split_ai = false  @analyst_ai_options
        assessment_stage.split_ai = false  @analyst_ai_options
    "High AI help":
        "At the end of AI progress, AI does 90% of the planning and 70% of the damage assessment for each
            target, both on the faster path."
        planning_stage.target_ai_end = 0.9  @analyst_ai_options
        assessment_stage.target_ai_end = 0.7  @analyst_ai_options
        assessment_stage.target_payload_path = false  @analyst_ai_options
    "Low AI help":
        "At the end of AI progress, AI does 60% of the planning and 50% of the damage assessment for each
            target, none of the review and the approval, and 20% of the assessment of the whole attack."
        planning_stage.target_ai_end = 0.6  @analyst_ai_options
        assessment_stage.target_ai_end = 0.5  @analyst_ai_options
        planning_stage.ai_end = 0  @analyst_ai_options
        assessment_stage.ai_end = 0.2  @analyst_ai_options
    "Slow planning of surveillance":
        "AI helps the analysts with each target of an attack, but the planning of a new access of surveillance
            moves only as the review and the approval of an attack do."
        surveillance_program.plan_target_weight = 0  @surveillance_planning_ai

options "Analysts' staffing":
    "Value of the work":
        "The analysts go first to the mission where one more analyst-year is worth more."
    "Work waiting":
        "The analysts' split follows each mission's share of the analysis work that it needs."
        analysts.by_value = false  @analyst_staffing
    "Fixed split":
        "The analysts' split stays at today's."
        analysts.fixed_split = true  @analyst_staffing

options "Workforce":
    "Fixed groups":
        "The four groups of experts keep their sizes for the whole period."
    "Idle operators retrain":
        "The leaders retrain operators who wait for the analysts as analysts, at half an analyst's work, over
            about three years."
        operators.retrains = true  @workforce

options "Campaign targets":
    "One objective":
        "The force masses its attacks on one military objective, whose targets share one defender."
    "Dispersed targets":
        "The force spreads its attacks over many unconnected targets that share no defender, and the plan
            counts on their total effect."
        defenders.common_spread = 0.13  @dispersed_targets
        defenders.shared_failure = 0.03  @dispersed_targets
        defenders.failure_rate = 0.24 per_year  @dispersed_targets
        military_planners.objective_share = 1  @dispersed_targets

options "Funding rule":
    "Current results":
        "The leaders fund attacks for the value that their results give now."
    "Results and lessons":
        "The leaders also fund attacks for the value of what the attacks teach."
        leadership.foresight = 1  @funding_rules

options "Funding surge":
    "No surge":
        "The leaders get no extra money for attacks."
    "The 2025 surge":
        "The leaders get USD 0.25 billion more for attacks in each year from 2026 to 2029."
        leadership.surge_funding = 0.25 USD2025_bn/yr  @surge_2025

options "Defender hardening":
    "No hardening":
        "The defenders' lasting capability stays as it is today."
    "Slow hardening":
        "The defenders get better every year, by 0.05 log-odds of an attack's success, as more organizations
            find intrusions themselves."
        defenders.hardening_rate = 0.05 per_year  @hardening
    "Defenders' AI":
        "The defenders' AI hardens their networks: at the end of AI progress it takes 0.5 log-odds of an
            attack's success."
        defenders.ai_hardening = 0.5  @defender_ai

options "Tempo":
    "Peacetime":
        "The country is at peace."
    "Wartime":
        "The country goes to war in 2026: the moment to use an attack held ready comes about monthly, an
            attack must land within a week of the decision, and the planners review every quarter."
        military_planners.war = true  @wartime

runs:
    ai_fast = "Slow patching" + "Fast AI progress" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "One objective" + "No
        hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · Fast AI progress"
    no_ai = "Slow patching" + "No AI progress" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "One objective" + "No
        hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · No AI progress"
    ai_slow = "Slow patching" + "Slow AI progress" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "One objective" + "No
        hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · Slow AI progress"
    ai_fast_lessons = "Slow patching" + "Fast AI progress" + "Results and lessons" + "No surge" + "One
        objective" + "No hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · Fast AI progress · Funding counts the lessons"
    surge_today = "Slow patching" + "No AI progress" + "Current results" + "The 2025 surge" + "One
        objective" + "No hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · No AI progress · The 2025 surge"
    ai_reversal = "Slow patching" + "AI progress, then costs rise" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "One
        objective" + "No hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · AI progress, then costs rise"
    dispersed = "Slow patching" + "Fast AI progress" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "Dispersed
        targets" + "No hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · Fast AI progress · Dispersed targets"
    dispersed_no_ai = "Slow patching" + "No AI progress" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "Dispersed
        targets" + "No hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · No AI progress · Dispersed targets"
    defenders_ai = "Slow patching" + "Fast AI progress" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "One
        objective" + "Defenders' AI" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · Fast AI progress · Defenders' AI"
    wartime = "Slow patching" + "No AI progress" + "Current results" + "No surge" + "One objective" + "No
        hardening" + "Wartime"
        "Slow patching · No AI progress · Wartime"
    analysts_one_share = "Slow patching" + "Fast AI progress" + "One AI share" + "Current results" + "No
        surge" + "One objective" + "No hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · Fast AI progress · One AI share for each stage of the analysts"
    slow_spy_planning = "Slow patching" + "Fast AI progress" + "Slow planning of surveillance" + "Current
        results" + "No surge" + "One objective" + "No hardening" + "Peacetime"
        "Slow patching · Fast AI progress · Slow planning of surveillance"

notes:
    premises:
        START: "The model starts in 2026 with today's split of the experts. Today's split is a rest point of
            the funding rule, so without AI the force stays where it starts. The numbers of today come from
            the United States, the one country with a public split of money and people."
    limitations:
        one-country: "The model follows one country. Other countries' attacks, and a race between countries,
            change the attention of defenders and the value of attacks in ways that the model does not
            follow."  @program_basis
        value-unit: "Value is in units of one expert-year of surveillance in 2026. The model compares the two
            missions; it gives no price of either."  @sev_definition
        assumed-ranges: "Most values are assumptions of this scenario, with ranges that a reader can explore.
            A range is not a measured interval."  @program_basis
    decisive: "Whether the lessons of attacks outlast their loss to patches, turnover and secrecy at the
        volume that cheaper attacks allow."
    reporting:
        deaths:
            category: deaths
        casualties:
            category: casualties
        economic_loss:
            category: loss
    not_estimated:
        deaths:
            label: "Deaths"
            reason: "The model follows the country's cyber programs, not the harm of each attack to
                people."  @harm_outside
        casualties:
            label: "Serious casualties, including deaths"
            reason: "The model follows the country's cyber programs, not the harm of each attack to
                people."  @harm_outside @hazus_severity
        economic_loss:
            label: "Economic loss"
            reason: "The model follows the country's cyber programs, not the loss that each attack
                causes."  @harm_outside
    comparisons:
        no_ai: ai_fast
        dispersed: dispersed_no_ai
        defenders_ai: ai_fast
        analysts_one_share: ai_fast
        slow_spy_planning: ai_fast

record research_basis: assumption "Researchers find flaws that the defenders do not know and build the tools
    that use them. One group serves surveillance and attacks, and its work goes to each pool as the pool needs
    it."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record research_share: assumption "Three in a hundred of the country's experts are researchers. No count is
    public, so the scenario chooses the share. Today's work of the researchers meets today's needs, so the
    results depend on its ratios."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record capability_reserve: assumption "Each pool keeps never-used capabilities for a year of the missions'
    draws from it. When a pool's never-used stock falls below about a week of its draws, the parts of each
    step that need a new zero-day slow down with it, and the missions start only the operations that they can
    equip. The scenario chooses both times."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record research_ai: assumption "AI finds flaws and builds tools. At the end of AI progress, a researcher finds
    ten times as many capabilities in a year as today. One model found and exploited zero-days in every major
    operating system and browser. Automated systems found 86% of the synthetic flaws of one contest. The
    scenario chooses the multiple."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-MYTHOS-FLAWS
        E-SC45-AIXCC
record research_split: assumption "Each pool asks the researchers for the never-used capabilities that the
    missions take from it and that the defenders find, and for what restores its reserve. The researchers do
    no more than the pools ask, while they can. So each never-used stock stays near its reserve, and today's
    pools are at rest."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record research_yield: identity "Today a researcher finds the needs of all of the pools over the researchers
    in a year. So the work of the researchers meets today's needs."
record operator_basis: assumption "Operators do the hands-on work of operations. On attacks they gain access,
    move inside the network, prepare the effect and execute it. On surveillance they gain access, move inside
    the network and deploy implants. The leaders move operators between the missions."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record operator_priority: assumption "The operators' hours go to the operations farthest along first. On
    attacks, execution comes first, then the effect, then movement inside the network, then initial access.
    Each step runs at the lower of its pace by time and the pace that its hours allow. So the force finishes
    the attacks underway before it starts new ones."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record expert_pools: identity "The groups of experts are fixed by default, and they add up to the experts.
    Today's experts on attacks are operators and analysts as the stages of an attack say. The researchers are
    part of the agency's experts. Its other experts are operators who deploy implants, analysts who plan new
    accesses, and collection specialists, in shares. So today's work sets the size of each group, and today's
    share of the operators on attacks follows from it."
record workforce: assumption "By default the four groups of experts keep their sizes for the whole period, so
    operators whose operations the analysts cannot plan wait, and the model reports them. As an option, the
    leaders retrain those operators as analysts: about two thirds of them move in three years, and each does
    half an analyst's work. No operator waits today, so today stays at rest. The scenario chooses these
    values; no source measures them."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record collection_basis: assumption "Collection specialists run collection on surveillance's deployed
    implants, translate, and turn the raw take into intelligence. They are the surveillance experts who
    neither deploy implants nor plan new accesses. In 2011 the implant program made full use of only an eighth
    of its machines with implants."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
    claims:
        E-SC45-GENIE-2011
record analyst_basis: assumption "Analysts plan the operations of both missions, assess the damage of attacks
    and use the intelligence. Their split between the missions moves toward each mission's share of the
    analysis work waiting. On attacks they assess the damage of the attacks made first, then plan new ones. So
    a mission whose work grows takes analysts from the other."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record analyst_split: assumption "The analysts' split moves toward the target of the staffing rule, about two
    thirds of the way in one year. On attacks, damage assessment takes at most its share of the analysis work
    waiting, and planning takes the rest. Today's split is a rest point of every staffing rule. The scenario
    chooses the time."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record analyst_staffing: assumption "The leaders staff the analysts by the value of their work. Each mission
    gets its analysis work first in proportion to the priority that the value of one more analyst-year gives
    it, and the split moves toward that target over the adjustment time. One more analyst- year is worth much
    more on attacks than on surveillance's planning, because the collection specialists, not the accesses,
    limit surveillance's take. The options keep the split by the work that each mission needs, or fixed at
    today's. Each rule gives today's split at rest. The scenario chooses the rule; no source measures it."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record analyst_load: assumption "Today's work fills 90% of the capacity of the analysts. So a small growth of
    the work does not slow it, and a large growth does. The scenario chooses the share."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record surveillance_analysts: assumption "Half of the surveillance experts are analysts, and a tenth of them
    plan new accesses. The rest of them process what the accesses collect, as collection specialists. The
    scenario chooses both shares."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record surveillance_planning_ai: assumption "To plan a new access of surveillance is analysis of one target,
    so by default AI helps it as fully as it helps the analysis of each target of an attack. With a share of
    0, its planning moves only as the review and the approval of an attack do. No source measures the planning
    work of an access, so the model reports results across the share."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record analysis_ai: assumption "AI does 10% of the collection specialists' processing of the take today and
    60% at the end of AI progress, on the slower path of AI progress: translation and triage. AI did most of
    the work of one espionage campaign, and that work included the sorting of the stolen data. The scenario
    chooses the shares."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-AI-CAMPAIGN
record capability_burn: assumption "An exposed attack burns the capabilities that it holds, and an attack that
    stays hidden keeps them for reuse. In a year the force makes the same share of the attacks that hold
    capabilities of a pool, so that share of the held capabilities leaves the pool's held stocks. Where
    surveillance also uses a burned capability, the defenders find 2% of the accesses that run on it. The
    leaders count each access that the defenders find at the value that one access gives in its life today.
    The scenario chooses the share."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record capability_pool: assumption "A capability is a flaw that the defenders do not know, with the tools that
    use it, and it burns as a whole. Each step has a pool: access and movement in the network serve both
    missions, the effect serves attacks and collection serves surveillance. A capability is never used, used
    by surveillance, used in an attack, or burned. Used in an attack, it is held by an attack underway, or
    kept from an earlier attack that was not exposed."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record one_day_chance: assumption "A need of a step takes no capability when a known flaw or the target's own
    functions serve it, on a target that has not fixed the flaw by its use. They can serve 80% of the needs of
    access and of the effect, and 90% of movement and collection. Industrial systems fix flaws at a fifth of
    the pace, and the systems inside a network at half. The scenario chooses the values."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
    claims:
        E-SC45-KEV-FIX
        E-SC45-KEV-2025
        E-SC45-DBIR-SATURATION
record capability_use: assumption "A step takes one capability for each kind of target system that no known
    flaw serves: one for each kind of system of an attack, and one for each access of surveillance. Each such
    zero-day is a capability already in use or a never-used one."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record capability_sources: assumption "Today a tenth of an attack's zero-days are capabilities that
    surveillance already uses, and a twentieth reuse a capability of an earlier attack that was not burned.
    Surveillance serves 95% of its zero-day needs with capabilities that it already uses, and one need in
    10,000 with a capability of an earlier attack. A capability in use serves a need as one independent try:
    the chance is one minus the exponential of minus the tries, and the tries grow in proportion to the
    capabilities in use. The rest of the needs take never-used capabilities. No count is public. The scenario
    chooses the shares."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record capability_rest: identity "Today each pool is at rest: each stock gains in a year the capabilities that
    it loses. So today's stocks follow from today's needs and shares, from the pace at which the force makes
    the attacks that hold them, and from the rate at which others find flaws. The checks reject shares that no
    rest point can keep."
record target_kinds: assumption "A further target of an attack runs a kind of system that the other targets do
    not with a chance of 10%. So an attack on 30 targets needs about four capabilities at a step, not 30. The
    scenario chooses the chance."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
record ai_path: assumption "AI progress reaches the cyber force on two paths: one for access, the running of
    attacks, the running of implants and the defenders, and a slower one for payloads, target analysis, damage
    assessment, the planning of new accesses and the processing of the take. Each is 1 - exp(-t / its time),
    times the pace. The reversal option takes back a share of both after a start time."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record ai_pace: assumption "The scenario assumes how fast AI progress reaches the cyber force. The default
    reaches about two thirds of the end values in 5 years; the options give 4 and 12 years."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record analyst_ai_options: assumption "The options test the analysts' AI shares. One AI share is the earlier
    form: one share for each stage of the analysts. High and low help take the ends of the ranges of the
    split: 90% and 70%, or 60% and 50%, of the work for each target at the end. In the low option AI does none
    of the review and the approval, and 20% of the assessment of the whole attack. Today is the same in every
    option."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record ai_reversal: assumption "The reversal option tests hysteresis: the costs of attacks rise again after 12
    years and take back 80% of AI progress. The scenario chooses these values to test whether the force stays
    where it got to; no source predicts them."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record no_ai_path: assumption "Without AI progress, every driver keeps its value of today: the run is the
    matched human pathway of the scenario."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record split_basis: assumption "The leaders split one pool of operators between the two missions. Each
    operator on attacks is an operator taken from surveillance."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
    claims:
        E-SC45-CARTER-ISIS
record experts_pool: assumption "The pool is the NSA workforce and the posts of Cyber Command's
    attack-oriented teams as designed. The NSA had about 39,000 people in 2024 and shed about 2,000 in 2025,
    so the pool is 37,000 + 3,535 = 40,535 people: researchers, operators, collection specialists and
    analysts. Not all of them are cyber experts, so the pool sets the scale of the model, and the results
    depend on ratios."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
    claims:
        E-SC45-NSA-WORKFORCE
        E-SC45-CMF-SIZE
record share_today: assumption "Today's share of the experts on attacks is the share of Cyber Command's
    attack-oriented posts in the pool: 3,535 / 40,535 = 0.087, a staff ratio of about 10.5:1. The range covers
    the ratios of staff (6.3:1 to 12.7:1) and money (5.4:1 to 8.9:1) in the workbook's sources."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
    claims:
        E-SC45-NSA-WORKFORCE
        E-SC45-CMF-SIZE
        E-SC45-CYBERCOM-BUDGET
record split_limits: assumption "The leaders keep a floor of operators on attacks, for strategy and readiness,
    whatever the results, and they never put more than a ceiling on attacks. Today about 58% of the operators
    who do the hands-on work of operations are on attacks, so the ceiling is 90%. The scenario chooses both."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
record funding_speed: assumption "Budgets and teams follow results slowly. The defense budget process starts
    more than two years before the money is spent, and trained teams take years to build. The scenario takes
    three years for the split to move about two thirds of the way to its target, with a range from one to six
    years."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
    claims:
        E-SC45-PPBE
record funding_response: assumption "The target split is a logistic function of the difference in returns
    between attacks and surveillance, between the floor and the ceiling. Equal returns keep today's split. The
    steepness says how strongly budgets follow results. In one study of US programs, 10 points on a 100-point
    performance score moved proposed budgets by 4 to 5%. If those 10 points stand for a difference in returns
    of 0.02 to 0.1, the steepness is about 0.8 to 4. The scenario takes 2, with a range from 0.5 to 10."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
    claims:
        E-SC45-PART-BUDGET
record funding_forms: assumption "The proportional form is the second form of the funding rule: the split
    moves at a rate proportional to the difference in returns, within its floor and ceiling, as in replicator
    dynamics."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
record funding_rules: assumption "Funding compares the assessed return of an operator on attacks with the
    return of an operator on surveillance, as a share of surveillance's current return. With foresight, it
    adds the value of the lessons of the operator's attacks."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
record discount_rate: assumption "The scenario assumes a discount rate of 3% a year for the future value of
    lessons, with a range from 2% to 10%."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
record budget_cycle: assumption "The leaders assess the results once a year, as a yearly budget does."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
record split_balance: identity "The operators on attacks and on surveillance add up to the operators. The
    share on attacks moves by two flows: the flow that raises it and the flow that lowers it."
record revealed_split: assumption "Today's split is a rest point of the funding rule, where an operator on
    attacks and an operator on surveillance return the same. The value of one intended effect follows from it:
    the value that makes today's returns equal. With foresight, the return includes the value of lessons. So
    the model calibrates value by the revealed choice of the country, not by the claims of the essay."
    assumption A-SC45-SPLIT
record sev_definition: identity "The unit of value is the yearly value of one expert on surveillance in 2026."
record surge_basis: assumption "A one-off surge of money buys extra experts for attacks while it lasts, at the
    cost of one expert-year. The model treats the money as extra capacity, not as money taken from
    surveillance."
    assumption A-SC45-SURGE
record surge_2025: assumption "The 2025 law sets aside USD 1 billion for offensive cyber operations, available
    through 2029: USD 0.25 billion a year for four years."
    assumption A-SC45-SURGE
    claims:
        E-SC45-SURGE-2025
record expert_cost: assumption "The scenario assumes USD 0.42 million for one expert-year: the resources of
    Cyber Command in FY2026, USD 2.6 billion, over the 6,187 people of the Cyber Mission Force."
    assumption A-SC45-SURGE
record assessment_noise: assumption "A yearly assessment of the value of attacks has an error in log units.
    One part, 0.8 for one outcome, falls with the targets hit and with the assessed outcomes, as an average
    does. The central run takes the median error, 0."
    assumption A-SC45-NOISE
record assessment_common: assumption "Part of the error of a yearly assessment is common to all of its
    outcomes, so it does not fall with their number: 0.3 log units. In the 1991 air campaign the services and
    their contractors shared one error: the claimed hit rate of one bomber was 80% against 41% to 60% in a
    later audit. The scenario chooses the value."
    assumption A-SC45-NOISE
    claims:
        E-SC45-DESERT-STORM-BDA
record assessment_bias: assumption "As an option, the bias of the assessment changes along the AI path: an AI
    that writes assessments can overstate, as one AI-orchestrated campaign made up credentials and claimed
    secret data that was public. A bias that does not change only rescales the value of an effect that today's
    split shows, so by default the bias does not change."
    assumption A-SC45-NOISE
    claims:
        E-SC45-AI-CAMPAIGN
record wartime: assumption "As an option, the country goes to war in 2026 from today's peacetime posture. In
    war the moment to use an attack held ready comes about monthly, an attack must land within a week of the
    decision, and the planners review every quarter. In 2022 Russia massed its destructive attacks at the
    war's outset and then spent its first stockpiles: 22 organizations were hit in the first week, about one a
    week from mid-April, and the tempo lasted only weeks. The scenario chooses the values."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
    claims:
        E-SC45-WARTIME-TEMPO
record surveillance_basis: assumption "Surveillance gains accesses in other countries' networks with
    capabilities from the pools, moves inside them and deploys implants. It gets value each year from the take
    that its collection specialists process, less the loss from alert defenders. It loses accesses to the
    defenders and to exposed attacks, and its operators gain new ones."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
record surveillance_accesses: assumption "Surveillance holds 85,000 accesses today: accesses gained and
    implants deployed on computers and networks. The agency had 68,975 machines with active implants in 2011
    and had deployed between 85,000 and 100,000 by 2014, from 100 to 150 in 2004. No later count is public, so
    the scenario takes the count of 2014 for today. The results depend on its ratios."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
    claims:
        E-SC45-IMPLANT-COUNT
        E-SC45-GENIE-2011
record surveillance_use: assumption "The collection specialists run only some of the implants, because people
    limit exploitation at a large scale. In 2011 the implant program made full use of 8,448 of its 68,975
    machines, 12%, and the scenario takes that share for today. The implants run are the implants times the
    reach of the collection specialists over their sum, so they are always fewer than either."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
    claims:
        E-SC45-TURBINE
        E-SC45-GENIE-2011
record collection_queue: assumption "The take of the implants waits in a queue until the collection
    specialists process it, about five weeks today. They process the take first and run collection with the
    hours left, so a backlog takes hours from collection. One implant-year of collection gives one access-year
    of take. No time is public. The scenario chooses it."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
record surveillance_builders: assumption "A twentieth of the surveillance experts are operators who gain
    access and deploy and keep implants: the implant program had 1,870 staff in 2011, against a pool of about
    37,000 experts today. The work of a new access is its initial access and the deployment that it will need,
    for the accesses that last until their deployment."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
    claims:
        E-SC45-GENIE-2011
record surveillance_builds: identity "Today's new accesses replace the accesses that surveillance loses, so
    today's accesses are a rest point. That sets the operators' work to gain one access and deploy its implant
    today. The defenders also find a few accesses through burned capabilities, so surveillance holds a little
    fewer accesses at rest than the builds alone keep. The work then moves with AI as the access work of an
    attack does, because it is the same work. The analysts plan the new accesses, so surveillance starts fewer
    when the analysts cannot plan all of them."
record surveillance_priority: assumption "The operators on surveillance deploy implants on the accesses that
    they have gained first, and gain new initial access with the hours left. Initial access and deployment
    split the operators' work to gain one access and deploy its implant as the access of an attack splits, and
    they take the same times."
    assumption A-SC45-EXPERTS
record surveillance_loss: assumption "Surveillance loses its accesses at 50% a year to the defenders, to
    patches and to changes. Espionage hides long: in the intrusions that one firm investigated in 2025,
    espionage stayed a median of 122 days before it was found, against 14 days for all intrusions, and one
    backdoor stayed nearly 400 days. Accesses that no one finds last longer. The scenario chooses the rate."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
    claims:
        E-SC45-ESPIONAGE-DWELL
record surveillance_loop: identity "An access moves from initial access to held, and becomes an implant when
    surveillance has moved inside the network and deployed it. Accesses held and implants leave when
    surveillance loses them or the defenders find them through burned capabilities. At rest, each stock is
    what enters it in a year over the rate at which it leaves."
record surveillance_returns: assumption "The value of surveillance grows as the take that the collection
    specialists process, to the power 0.8: each extra access adds less. They process what the implants that
    they run collect, as far as they can. Today the value is one expert-year of surveillance for each expert.
    The scenario chooses the exponent."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
record surveillance_alert: assumption "Alert defenders lower the value of surveillance less than the value of
    attacks, because surveillance stays hidden. The scenario chooses the factor."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
record surveillance_ai: assumption "AI does a growing share of the work of running implants: 30% today,
    because the automated control of implants in groups has run since 2010, and 90% at the end of AI progress,
    as in one AI-orchestrated espionage campaign. AI work costs supervision, which the implants that one
    collection specialist runs at once share, and compute, as in the stages of an attack. So the gain of
    surveillance from AI is a result, and the implants deployed limit it."
    assumption A-SC45-SURVEILLANCE
    claims:
        E-SC45-TURBINE
        E-SC45-AI-CAMPAIGN
record defender_basis: assumption "The defenders adapt in three parts. Their attention follows the threat flow
    that they answer, of which the force's attacks are a small share, saturates and fades within months; it
    lowers the log-odds of an attack's success and the value of surveillance. They fix what an attack exposes,
    so an attack that reuses it may fail. As an option, their lasting capability grows with time and with
    their own AI."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
record threat_flow: assumption "The defenders answer the whole threat flow: 884 flaws were first seen
    exploited in 2025, and 90 zero-days were exploited in the wild, from many actors. The force's attacks are
    5% of the threat that they answer today, counted in targets, and the rest of the flow stays as it is. The
    scenario chooses the share."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-KEV-2025
        E-SC45-ZERODAY-2025
record attention_cap: assumption "Attention saturates. When the flaws in one dataset grew from 69 million to
    527 million in three years, the median time to fix an exploited flaw rose from 32 to 43 days in a year,
    the share fully fixed fell from 38% to 26%, and 60% to 70% stayed open after a week whatever the maturity
    of the organization. So attention rises with the threat flow towards a cap, six times today's, 0.3
    log-odds: no data show a larger drop. The scenario chooses the cap."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-DBIR-SATURATION
record alertness_today: assumption "Today's attention is a rest point: today's threat flow draws the defenders
    to today's attention, 0.05 log-odds. No study measures it; values much above 0.1 would imply drops in
    success at high attack rates that no data show."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
record alertness_fades: assumption "Attention fades at 2 a year. Two actors that a security firm exposed
    returned to their earlier activity after about five months, and quickly moved to new infrastructure. The
    scenario chooses the rate."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-APT1-RETURN
record alertness_balance: identity "Attention moves towards the level that the threat flow draws, at the rate
    at which it fades: one flow raises it and the other lowers it."
record outcome_correlation: assumption "The targets of one attack share steps: one access path, one tool, one
    command. When a shared step works, each target still succeeds or fails on its own; when it fails, all fail
    together. Today the correlation is 0.85: in documented attacks, the targets that shared the decisive step
    fell together. A share of the log-chance of success lies in the shared steps, so the correlation follows
    from it. Lessons do not change the shared share, so the correlation stays at today's chance of success: an
    approximation that keeps the analysis of rest points simple."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        V-C01
record common_factor: assumption "Attacks massed on one objective face one defender, its national CERT and a
    few security vendors. So the log-odds of a plan's success move together around the plan: by 0.3 by
    default, with a range from 0.1 to 0.46. Against one defender, the monthly hit share of a drone campaign
    moved by about 0.27 to 0.46 in log-odds; unconnected victims of ransomware moved together by at most about
    0.13 a quarter. All of those drones were one type of weapon, so the drone figure can also hold a part from
    the attacker's side. The steps that the attacks themselves share are a separate step that can fail."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-SHAHED-2026
record shared_failure: assumption "A capability that the attacks of a plan share, such as one tool, one access
    path or one channel of command, can fail for all of the attacks that use it at once: at the start of the
    plan with a chance of 5%, and while it runs at a rate of 0.6 a year, as the defenders find it. Each kind
    of target system needs its own such capability, and each fails on its own with today's chance, so the
    number of failures in a plan is Poisson. Each failure takes its share of the plan. Such failures are all
    or nothing, so the model counts them as a mixture over their number and not as a correlation. The scenario
    chooses the values."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
record shared_depth: assumption "A failed shared capability takes the attacks that depend on it, and they give
    no effect. Each kind of target system in an attack needs its own capability. So one failure takes a
    smaller share of a plan as the kinds of target system grow, but more capabilities can fail: each kind's
    capability fails on its own. The scenario assumes that one failure takes half of today's plan, which has
    one kind."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record plan_concentration: assumption "Today half of a plan's effect depends on one capability that its
    attacks share: half of today's attacks reuse a flaw, tool or infrastructure that an earlier attack
    exposed. One state actor built a new variant of its 2016 tool from the same source code, and at least nine
    of 18 zero-days exploited in early 2022 were variants of patched flaws. The scenario chooses the share."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-INDUSTROYER2
        E-SC45-ZERODAY-VARIANTS
record dispersed_targets: assumption "Unconnected targets share no defender, so their log-odds move together
    by about 0.13, the bound that ransomware victims show, and a shared step fails less often. The plan counts
    on the total effect of all of the force's attacks. The option tests the essay's claim that AI makes many
    small, unconnected attacks reliable in total. Across campaigns, the success of mass attacks on unconnected
    victims through one flaw still fell as the victims' defenses matured."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-COVEWARE-CAMPAIGNS
record patch_tiers: assumption "The fast defenders lose the force's advance access and surveillance's accesses
    twice as fast, keep their attention twice as long and start with twice the attention, and they fix a known
    flaw at 15 a year, the pace at which most servers fixed one famous flaw within three weeks. The scenario
    chooses these values."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-PROXYLOGON-FIX
record rediscovery: assumption "AI helps the defenders find and close flaws: in every run, discovery and
    patching rise with AI progress, to three times today's rates at the end. In one competition, AI systems
    found 86% of the synthetic flaws and patched 68% of those. The scenario chooses the growth."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-AIXCC
record loss_routes: assumption "A flaw that the force holds is lost in three ways: others find it on their own
    and disclose it, a patch or code change made for another reason closes it, or its systems leave service or
    stop mattering. For a stockpiled flaw the three together give the 14.5% a year of a 6.9-year life.
    Independent rediscovery is 5.7% a year of it, and the scenario splits the rest evenly between patching and
    irrelevance, because the study gives no split. A flaw in use can also be seen at work: zero-days used in
    attacks lasted about 312 days before their disclosure, so the scenario takes 1.17 a year for a flaw in
    use, an upper bracket for a careful force. AI speeds discovery and patching in every run, up to three
    times by the end of AI progress; irrelevance does not change."
    assumption A-SC45-CAPABILITIES
    claims:
        E-SC45-ZERODAY-LIFE
        E-SC45-ZD-LONGEVITY
        E-SC45-ZD-COLLISION
        E-SC45-ZD-LIFE-STATUS
        E-SC45-ZD-IN-USE-LIFE
record hardening: assumption "As an option, the defenders' lasting capability grows by 0.05 log-odds of an
    attack's success a year: organizations first found the intrusions themselves in 52% of one firm's
    investigations of 2025, up from 43% in 2024, while the median dwell rose from 11 to 14 days. The default
    has none, so the run without AI stays at rest. The scenario chooses the rate."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-INTERNAL-DETECTION
        E-SC45-ESPIONAGE-DWELL
record defender_ai: assumption "As an option, the defenders' AI hardens their networks: it takes 0.5 log-odds
    of an attack's success at the end of AI progress. AI systems found 86% of the synthetic flaws of one
    competition and patched 68% of those, in 45 minutes on average at about USD 152 a task, and one model
    found thousands of serious flaws. Fixes across organizations have not sped up, so the default has no
    hardening. AI's help to find and close flaws is in every run."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-AIXCC
        E-SC45-MYTHOS-FLAWS
record politics_basis: assumption "An attributed attack draws sanctions or replies. The expected cost of one
    attack is the chance of attribution times the cost of an attributed attack."
    assumption A-SC45-POLITICS
    claims:
        E-SC45-NOTPETYA-ATTRIBUTION
        E-SC45-NOTPETYA-SANCTIONS
record attribution_channels: assumption "Other countries attribute an attack by four kinds of evidence: its
    code and tools, its infrastructure, its operators' habits, and its choice of targets and time. An attack
    stays unattributed only when every kind misses, so the chance of attribution is one less the product of
    the misses: 0.73 today. Technical attribution of significant attacks runs about 0.6 to 0.95, and every
    large destructive state attack of recent years was attributed."
    assumption A-SC45-POLITICS
    claims:
        E-SC45-NOTPETYA-ATTRIBUTION
        E-SC45-POLAND-2025
record tools_channel: assumption "AI writes new code for each attack, so the code and tools of an attack
    attribute it far less often: 40% today, 5% at the end of AI progress. In the Polish attacks of 2025, a
    wiper that AI may have written could not be used for attribution, while the attack's infrastructure still
    overlapped with a known cluster."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-POLAND-2025
record infrastructure_channel: assumption "The servers and accounts of an attack attribute it 30% of the time
    today, and AI does not change that. The operators' habits and the choice of targets each attribute it 20%
    of the time."
    assumption A-SC45-POLITICS
record sanction_cost: assumption "The scenario assumes the cost of the sanctions and replies to one attributed
    attack: 10 expert-years of surveillance value."
    assumption A-SC45-POLITICS
    claims:
        E-SC45-NOTPETYA-SANCTIONS
record escalation: assumption "With escalation, the cost of sanctions grows with the attributed attacks in a
    year. The default has none. Formal replies to cyber attacks are few, and an escalation is more a threshold
    than a steady rise. So the range stops at 0.01 years for each attack: at today's tempo of about 260
    attributed attacks a year, that multiplies the cost of each attributed attack by about 3.6."
    assumption A-SC45-POLITICS
record planning_basis: assumption "Planners build plans around cyber attacks only when a plan of attacks meets
    its plan reliably: when the chance that it hits the planned share of targets, less a tolerance, passes a
    level that the planners accept. One use of an attack is not doctrine: doctrine needs reviews that pass
    again and again."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record plan_test: assumption "A plan counts on the attacks that the force can mass on one objective in its
    time. The planners test plans of four lengths, from one day to one quarter, by one rule, and a review
    passes when the best of them meets its plan often enough. So the model does not choose what doctrine
    becomes: the length that doctrine forms around is a result."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record plan_lengths: assumption "The plans run for one day, one week, one month and one quarter: from a salvo
    that opens an operation to a long campaign. The scenario chooses the lengths."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record held_capabilities: identity "The attacks that the force holds ready are a stock, and each keeps the
    targets, kinds of target system and correlation that it was built with. An attack built in advance goes
    into the stock when it is ready, and leaves it when its moment comes. At rest the stock is the attacks of
    a year that need access built in advance, times their mean wait. A plan can use these attacks and the
    attacks that the force finishes in the plan's time and that the pools can equip."
record objective_share: assumption "One objective can draw on a share of the force's attacks, because the
    force serves several commands and adversaries. The scenario chooses 20%, with a range from 5% to all of
    them."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record forecast_error: assumption "The planners do not know the share of targets that a plan will hit. Their
    error has a floor that lessons do not remove, 10% by default and up to 30%, and a part that the force's
    assessed outcomes reduce: the sampling error of the chance of success from those outcomes, not from the
    prior. After the 1991 air campaign, the claimed hit rate of one bomber was 80%, against 41 to 60% that a
    later audit found."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
    claims:
        E-SC45-DESERT-STORM-BDA
record plan_tolerance: assumption "The planners accept a shortfall of 25% from the planned share of targets
    hit, and need a chance of 80% to meet the plan. Planners guard against a shortfall with redundancy, and an
    effect above the plan does not break it. The evidence brackets the ranges: a chance of 75% to 95%, higher
    for effects on which other parts of an operation depend, and a shortfall of 20% to 50%. As an option, the
    test of the earlier model also fails a plan that hits more than the tolerance above it."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record plan_spread: assumption "The share of targets that a plan hits varies with the luck of each target, the
    shared causes of the targets of one attack, the common factor of the plan and the planners' error. The
    planned share is the mean share, because the planners learn it from pooled outcomes. The chance to meet
    the plan is a normal probability of the sum, mixed over the number of shared capabilities that fail. After
    a failure, only the luck of the attacks that are left counts."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record doctrine_time: assumption "Military plans count on cyber attacks after three planning reviews in a row
    pass, with a range from 1 to 10. The planners review once a year in peace. Reliance on a new weapon took
    one to two years in war and decades in peace."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record doctrine_lapse: assumption "Doctrine lapses after two reviews in a row in which every plan misses, with
    a range from 1 to 6. A guided shell whose hits fell from more than 50% to under 10% under jamming lost its
    place in plans within months. Doctrine can form again after more passes."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
    claims:
        E-SC45-EXCALIBUR
record doctrine_feedback: assumption "By default doctrine changes no value: it only shows when plans count on
    attacks. The option of a doctrine value tests a loop in which doctrine raises the value of effects."
    assumption A-SC45-PLANNING
record program_basis: assumption "One country with four groups of experts and four pools of capabilities. The
    amounts that change are the split of the operators and the split of the analysts; five stocks of an
    attack's targets and of attacks, from initial access to damage assessment; and four stocks of
    surveillance, from initial access to the take that waits to be processed. They are also six stocks of each
    pool of capabilities, two stocks of lessons, of effects and of access, and the attention of the defenders.
    The drivers of AI change over time."
    assumption A-SC45-STRUCTURE
record cost_today: identity "Today's work of one attack is the sum of the work of its stages today. The sum is
    a check, not a target: today's 3,535 attack posts over about 231 operations a year give 15 person-years,
    and the staff of the access program over the same operations give about 8."
    claims:
        E-SC45-OPS-2011
        E-SC45-CMF-SIZE
        E-SC45-GENIE-2011
record stage_basis: assumption "An attack needs five kinds of work: target analysis and approval, access to
    the targets, building and testing the effect, running the attack, and damage assessment. Access is two
    steps: initial access and movement inside the network. Each kind has work for the attack and work for each
    target, a share that AI does and a time. The cost of an attack, the time to build it and AI's share of its
    work follow from them. Analysts do the target analysis and the damage assessment, and operators do the
    rest."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
record stage_work: assumption "Each kind of work has expert work by hand for the attack and for each of its
    targets. The scenario sets the values from public anchors, stage by stage. Their sum today is a check
    against the evidence, not a target."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
record stage_cost: identity "The work of a stage for one attack is its work by hand times its cost share, and
    times the cost of waiting when its product waits ready for use."
record stage_ai: assumption "AI does a share of each kind of work. A unit of AI work still costs an expert's
    supervision, which the attacks that one expert runs at once share, and the compute that it uses. So
    supervising attacks in parallel saves only the work that AI does."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record stage_paths: assumption "AI progress reaches access, the running of attacks and the analysis of each
    target faster than the building of payloads, the review and the approval of an attack and damage
    assessment. AI has done most of the tactical work of an espionage campaign, while the most complex
    intrusions and attacks on industrial systems stay mostly manual. The slower path reaches about two thirds
    of its end in 10 years by default."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record stage_split: assumption "The analysts' work has two parts. The work for each target is the analysis of
    the target and the check of the effect on it. The work for the whole attack is the legal review, the
    approval and the assessment of the whole effect. AI can do more of the work for each target, and sooner,
    while policy sets how much of the review and the approval AI does: in kinetic targeting, AI cut the staff
    of target work by up to a hundred times, but approval still needs human judgment, and its time changed
    only by delegation. So each stage of the analysts has one AI share for each part, and each part has its
    own AI path. The scenario chooses this split; the operators' stages keep one share."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-WF-MAVEN-EXERCISE
        E-SC45-AN-HUMAN-JUDGMENT
        E-SC45-AN-CIA-APPROVAL
record stage_supervision: source_transfer "In one AI-orchestrated espionage campaign, AI did 80% to 90% of the
    tactical work against about 30 targets, and humans decided at a few points. So the scenario takes 0.2
    expert-years of supervision for each expert-year of AI work when an expert runs one attack at a time, and
    ten attacks at once at the end of AI progress."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-AI-CAMPAIGN
record stage_compute: assumption "An expert-year is about 2,000 working hours. One AI-built exploit chain that
    experts said would take them weeks cost under USD 2,000 of compute: about USD 25 for each expert-hour of
    80, or USD 0.05 million for an expert-year. A 20-hour attack range took a budget of 100 million tokens,
    and the model solved it in 3 of 10 tries, so a finished task costs about three times one try. The scenario
    takes USD 0.1 million for each expert-year of AI work today, and a tenth of that at the end of AI
    progress."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-OP-MYTHOS-COST
        E-SC45-AISI-RANGE
record planning_stage: assumption "Target analysis, legal review and approval take 1 expert-year for an attack
    and half an expert-year for each target. Approval of one operation has taken a series of meetings at the
    top of the government. Policy, not AI, sets the pace of the review and the approval: a delegation of 2018
    cut the approval of cyber operations from as much as a year to weeks, and US policy keeps human judgment
    over the use of force. So AI does none of the work for the attack today and 20% at the end."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-GLOWING-SYMPHONY
        E-SC45-AN-CIA-APPROVAL
        E-SC45-AN-NSPM13-SPEED
        E-SC45-AN-HUMAN-JUDGMENT
record planning_ai: assumption "AI does 20% of the target analysis for each target today and 75% at the end of
    AI progress, on the faster path. About 20,000 people already use one AI targeting system. In a
    demonstration, 20 soldiers with such a tool did the workload of a targeting cell of more than 2,000 in
    2003, and the imagery agency set the goal to automate 75% of the tasks of its imagery analysts. In a
    controlled test, soldiers with an AI tool got 18.2 points against 11.5 in the same time. These gains mix
    AI with new ways of work and policy, and cyber targets have no public equivalent, so the scenario takes
    less than the largest gain. It chooses values in the range 0.1 to 0.3 today and 0.6 to 0.9 at the end, and
    keeps the end at 0.9 or less so that a human still checks each target: observers warn that a fast review
    can become a formality."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-AN-MAVEN-USERS
        E-SC45-WF-MAVEN-EXERCISE
        E-SC45-AN-NGA-75
        E-SC45-AN-BUNDESWEHR
        E-SC45-AN-IRAN-REVIEW
record access_stage: assumption "Access takes 0.3 expert-years for an attack and 1.2 for each target, and
    about half a year today. In a test range without defenders, an AI model took over a 32-step network that
    would take an expert about 20 hours, in 3 of 10 tries, and an automated framework made working exploits
    for about half of the recent known flaws that it tried, at about USD 3 each. At the end of AI progress AI
    does 87% of the work, and access takes days."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-AISI-RANGE
        E-SC45-CVE-GENIE
record access_split: assumption "Initial access takes half of the time and of the work of access, and movement
    inside the network to the systems that the effect needs takes the other half. The scenario chooses the
    share."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
record payload_stage: assumption "Building and testing the effect takes 1.6 expert-years for an attack and 0.4
    for each target, and about 2.5 months today. A core team of five to ten people worked six months on one
    famous industrial payload, without its tests and management; a later one was built in as little as two
    months and was ready three weeks before its use. AI does 5% of the work today and 57% at the end, when it
    takes about 3.5 weeks."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-STUXNET-TEAM
        E-SC45-SANDWORM-2022
record execution_stage: assumption "Running the attack takes 0.4 expert-years for an attack and 0.1 for each
    target. One automated plan damaged devices in order in many networks at once. AI does 30% of the work
    today and 90% at the end."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-POLAND-2025
record assessment_stage: assumption "Damage assessment takes 1 expert-year for an attack and 0.7 for each
    target, and two assessments of one operation came 30 and 120 days after its start. AI does none of the
    work for the attack today and 30% at the end."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-GLOWING-SYMPHONY
record assessment_ai: assumption "AI does 10% of the damage check for each target today and 60% at the end of
    AI progress, on the slower path. In kinetic war, an AI battle system has verified more than 130,000
    destroyed or damaged targets, and the US Air Force asks for automatic assessment at once after a strike,
    because the reports now come hours later. Cyber Command says that AI cut its analysis of network traffic
    from hours, days or weeks to minutes and hours. That is defensive work, and the effect of a cyber attack
    is harder to see than a hit target, so the scenario takes the slower path. It chooses values in the range
    0.05 to 0.2 today and 0.5 to 0.7 at the end."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
    claims:
        E-SC45-AN-DELTA
        E-SC45-AN-BDA-HOURS
        E-SC45-AN-CYBERCOM-TRAFFIC
        E-SC45-GLOWING-SYMPHONY
record lead_time: assumption "The time to build an attack is the sum of the times of initial access, of
    movement inside the network and of building and testing the effect: about 9 months today, and about a
    month at the end of AI progress. It is the mean time that a target spends in the three stocks before its
    attack is ready. In documented operations, first known access came 2 to 11 months before the effect."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-POLAND-2025
record waiting_cost: assumption "An attack whose build takes longer than the warning needs access built in
    advance. Such an attack waits ready for its moment, needs upkeep and loses its access to patches and
    changes. The force builds lost access again while the attack waits: the model counts the work of that
    build and not its time. At rest, this work and the upkeep make the cost of waiting."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-VOLT-PREPOSITION
record access_decay: assumption "Access built in advance is lost to patches and changes at 30% a year. A
    privately held zero-day lives 6.9 years on average before its disclosure, about 15% a year, and access
    also breaks when the target's network changes. The scenario chooses the rate."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-ZERODAY-LIFE
record cost_learning: assumption "Lessons of attacks save part of the work of the stages that only attacks do:
    30% when the force knows all it can learn. The access stage learns from the lessons of access instead. The
    scenario chooses the share."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
record access_lessons: assumption "The work of access learns from the accesses that attacks build and from the
    accesses that surveillance gains, as far as the two tasks overlap: 70%, the overlap of the tasks of two
    models of one aircraft. Each doubling of the lessons of access saves 10% of the work of access, half the
    20% for each doubling of output in industry. The lessons of access fade at 20% a year: a privately held
    zero-day lives 6.9 years on average before its disclosure, about 15% a year, and staff leave.
    Surveillance's own work to build an access does not learn in the model. The scenario chooses the values."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
    claims:
        E-SC45-BENKARD-LEARNING
        E-SC45-ZERODAY-LIFE
record exposure_basis: assumption "When the defenders expose an attack, it burns the capabilities that it
    holds; an attack that stays hidden keeps them for reuse. No source gives the chance of exposure. The
    scenario takes 25%, so that the force burns about 20 to 40 capabilities a year: a part of the 63 to 106
    zero-days that defenders catch in use worldwide each year, from all actors, none of them attributed to the
    United States."
    assumption A-SC45-COSTS
    claims:
        E-SC45-ZD-2024-COUNT
        E-SC45-ZERODAY-2025
        E-SC45-ZD-2023-ACTORS
        E-SC45-ZD-2024-ACTORS
        E-SC45-ZD-2025-ACTORS
record known_flaws: assumption "A known flaw works only on a target that has not fixed it by the time the
    force gets access: a quarter of targets never fix it, and the others fix it at 1.5 a year, the median of
    about six months for exploited flaws in large scans. So the faster AI builds access, the more targets are
    still open."
    assumption A-SC45-DEFENDERS
    claims:
        E-SC45-KEV-FIX
        E-SC45-PROXYLOGON-FIX
record tailoring: assumption "AI tailors the shared steps of an attack to each target, so its targets fall
    together less often: at the end of AI progress, AI tailors 80% of those steps. The scenario chooses the
    share."
    assumption A-SC45-AI
record targets_basis: assumption "One attack hits one target today. With AI, one attack hits about 30 targets
    at once. The scenario chooses both."
    assumption A-SC45-RETURNS
    claims:
        E-SC45-POLAND-2025
        E-SC45-AI-CAMPAIGN
record success_basis: assumption "Today an attack gives its intended effect on a target one time in five. With
    every lesson learned, seven times in ten. The model moves between the two in log-odds, so the chance stays
    between 0 and 1."
    assumption A-SC45-RETURNS
    claims:
        V-C01
        E-SC45-STUXNET
        E-SC45-POLAND-2025
record value_scale: assumption "By default the value of an effect is the value that today's split shows. The
    scale tests a country that values effects more or less than its split shows."
    assumption A-SC45-RETURNS
record diminishing_value: assumption "The most valuable targets go first, so each effect is worth less as the
    targets hit in a year grow. The scenario chooses the scale."
    assumption A-SC45-RETURNS
record value_learning: assumption "Lessons also raise the value of an effect: better targets and better
    timing. The value grows by the factor 1 + value_learning when every lesson is learned, and by that factor
    to the power of the gain on the way, so it stays positive when lessons fall below today's. The scenario
    chooses the gain."
    assumption A-SC45-RETURNS
record value_basis: assumption "The value of a year's attacks is the value of an effect times the targets hit,
    with diminishing returns, the gain from lessons and, as an option, the gain from doctrine."
    assumption A-SC45-RETURNS
    claims:
        E-SC45-NOTPETYA-DAMAGE
record risk_value: assumption "Leaders who are averse to risk count less of a spread value: the value divided
    by 1 plus half the aversion times the relative variance. By default the leaders count the expected value."
    assumption A-SC45-RETURNS
record attack_count: identity "The force starts attacks at the rate that the work of its operators allows: the
    operators on attacks over the operators' work of one attack. That work counts the cost of waiting. The
    analysts plan each attack after they assess the damage of the attacks made, so the force starts fewer when
    they cannot plan all of them."
record attack_pipeline: identity "An attack's targets move through stocks: initial access, access inside the
    network, and positioned on the systems that the effect needs. The effect then turns the targets of one
    attack into one attack. An attack built on demand is made when it is ready; an attack built in advance
    waits ready for its moment. Each step runs at the lower of its stock over its time and the pace that its
    hours allow, in one part for each source of the capabilities that it needs. So the mean time that a target
    spends in a stock is that stock's time while the hours suffice."
record assessment_time: assumption "The damage assessment of an attack takes about four months today. One
    operation had a first assessment after 30 days, which could not yet assess the overall effect, and a
    second after 120 days. The lessons of an attack count when its assessment ends. At the end of AI progress
    the assessment takes half that time; the scenario chooses that value. When the analysts cannot do all of
    the work, the assessment takes longer."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
    claims:
        E-SC45-GLOWING-SYMPHONY
record assessment_basis: assumption "A damage assessment keeps part of what an outcome teaches: 40%, its
    chance to get an outcome right. In the 1991 air campaign the claimed hit rate of one bomber was 80%
    against 41% to 60% in a later audit, and the research notes put the reliability of two air campaigns'
    assessments near 0.3, so the range runs from 0.2 to 0.6. The scenario chooses the value."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
    claims:
        E-SC45-CARTER-ISIS
        E-SC45-DESERT-STORM-BDA
record learning_basis: assumption "The force learns from the assessed outcomes of its attacks when their
    assessment ends. The outcomes of the targets of one attack teach less than as many attacks, because they
    share causes."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
record learning_curve: assumption "Lessons get weight in the force's choices as they grow against a prior
    strength: with shape 1, the Bayesian weight of evidence of that strength. The scenario chooses 5,000
    assessed outcomes, so today's lessons have about 9% of the weight and a few attacks teach little. With
    this strength today's split is a stable rest point, as two decades of a marginal effects program suggest.
    A weaker prior with a steeper curve can make it unstable: with a prior of about 500 or less and a shape
    above about 2, today is a tipping point between two regimes."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
record learning_forms: assumption "The exponential curve is the second form of the learning curve."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
record lessons_today: assumption "Today's lessons are a rest point: what today's attacks teach in a year over
    the rate at which lessons fade."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
record forgetting: assumption "The force loses its lessons of effects at 30% a year to patches, burned tools,
    staff turnover and secrecy that limits sharing. These are the skills that only attacks practice, so they
    fade faster than the lessons of access, which surveillance also practices. The scenario chooses the rate."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
record burned_lessons: assumption "As an option, a share of today's loss of lessons comes from exposed attacks
    that burn their tools, so that share grows with the attacks."
    assumption A-SC45-LEARNING
record lesson_value: identity "The value of a lesson is the change of the yearly net value of attacks with one
    more lesson, over the discount rate plus the rate at which lessons fade. Where the analysts cannot plan
    all of the attacks, one more operator adds fewer attacks, and lessons also save the analysts' work."
record learning_balance: identity "The lessons rise with the flow of assessed outcomes and fall with the flow
    of lessons lost."
record period_start: assumption "The period starts in 2026. No attack starts it: the first move is the start
    of the period."
    assumption A-SC45-STRUCTURE
record harm_outside: assumption "The model does not follow the harm of attacks to people or the economy."
    assumption A-SC45-STRUCTURE
record hazus_severity: convention "Serious casualties are the people who die and the people who survive with
    serious harm that lasts: the Hazus severity levels S4 and S3."
    convention HAZUS-SEVERITY
